  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Mobile First**\n\nI\'m focusing on a mobile-first approach for this web app. Clean, device-specific designs are crucial from the outset. I\'m prioritizing separate, clean designs for each device type to ensure a seamless user experience, and to avoid retrofitting later.\n\n\n**Analyzing Feature Priorities**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the core features. Google account integration for sign-up and sign-in is essential, along with a crucial admin role. I want the UI to be slick and intuitive, with smooth navigation and dark mode support. Users should be able to organize their work with custom themes, categories, and color-coded notes. I\'m visualizing the writing displayed as cards, with key metadata and \'star\' counts. Lightning-fast search is non-negotiable, and I\'m also planning for seamless offline access and cross-device syncing. Also a simplified theme is better than fully customizable, so the user can just select some pre-set colors.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Appeal**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the UI/UX design, aiming for a Gen Z aesthetic: sleek, quirky, and polished. The goal is visual cohesion with themed icons, like bows or stars, and custom widgets. I\'m prioritizing user-friendliness and ease of use, keeping functionality straightforward, and also planning learning documentation. I\'m focusing on the plan-aggressively-then-implement strategy, keeping the coding simple. I plan to use Vercel and Supabase free tiers initially.\n\n\n**Formulating Targeted Questions**\n\nI\'m now formulating some critical questions. First, I need to clarify the backend and authentication architecture, and how I can utilize Google Auth, offline capabilities, and cross-device syncing within the constraints of free Vercel and Supabase tiers, to keep things simple. Then, I need to better understand the desired visual aesthetic and theme presets, so I can craft the right UI/UX. Finally, I\'ll need to know more about the \"Writer\" functionality, as a key feature.\n\n\n**Exploring Feature Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now thinking about the writing experience options: A distraction-free typewriter mode, or a rich, multimedia block editor? Also, I\'m considering an interactive developer guide: should this be a dedicated tab or a floating inspector? I\'m also now reviewing the question formatting rules for asking targeted questions, to make sure I get the right information.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_382460"
      name: "ask_question"
      arguments_json: "{\"questions\":[{\"is_multi_select\":false,\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Coquette, Y2K stars, matcha, and midnight dark vibes\",\"Minimalist modern monochrome with subtle pastel accents\",\"Retro vintage typewriter and parchment paper aesthetics\"],\"question\":\"Which visual theme and icon set should be the primary default style for the app?\"},{\"is_multi_select\":false,\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Distraction-free typewriter with word count and stats\",\"Rich visual cards with mood tags and reading time\",\"Split-screen live preview with dual reader and editor\"],\"question\":\"How would you prefer the writing and editing interface to be presented?\"},{\"is_multi_select\":false,\"options\":[\"(Recommended) Dedicated Dev Academy tab with interactive architecture visualizer\",\"Slide-out learning drawer with dev notes and checklists\"],\"question\":\"How should the built-in app development documentation and learning guide be structured?\"}],\"toolAction\":\"Asking clarifying questions\",\"toolSummary\":\"Ask clarifying questions about theme, editor, and guide\"}"
