  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visibility Challenges**\n\nI\'ve been examining the current light mode colors, and I find they hinder readability significantly. My goal is to revamp the design for improved visual clarity and coherence. The present iteration is simply not meeting the visibility requirements. I need to make the designs much better, and i want the designs to be visible.\n\n\n**Refining UI Design Concepts**\n\nI\'m now focusing on bolder themes and more unique designs for each. I\'m moving beyond simple color swaps to distinct designs related to their themes, and the emoji replacements with library icons are underway. I\'m giving extra attention to UI design and considering Gen Z-inspired artwork elements. I\'m seeking ideas and inspiration from products with visually appealing, thematic design to implement the cute designs that I\'m aiming for.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Readability and Contrast**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing readability with clean off-white canvas backgrounds for improved readability. I\'m focusing on deep, high-contrast text using solid dark shades with WCAG AAA readability, and ensuring subdued secondary text is a solid gray. I\'m also implementing strong, crisp card borders to create distinct surface boundaries.\n\n\n**Crafting Distinct Graphic Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into creating custom visual elements! I\'m moving beyond basic icons and into thematic SVG vector art, crafting unique illustrations for each theme. I\'m replacing emojis with hand-drawn SVG art for a more cohesive aesthetic. For example, the Coquette theme will feature beautiful silk bows and delicate heart seals, while Cyber Y2K will get chrome starbursts and holographic badges. I will also make each theme have distinctive graphic cards and watermark/sticker motifs.\n\n\n**Designing Thematic Banners**\n\nI\'m now implementing bold Gen Z-inspired design with neo-brutalist borders and thematic corner badges, inspired by platforms like Notion and Pinterest. I\'m focusing on hand-drawn stamps and illustrated scenes for each theme, like ribbon bows for Coquette and starlight for Y2K. I will also incorporate graphic stickers, such as \"Staff Pick\" and \"Midnight Verse.\"\n\n**Calibrating Font and Contrast**\n\nI am now making sure the font sizes and contrast are optimal. I\'m choosing bold, elegant title fonts and highly legible body fonts with strong contrast for the best visibility. The dark mode will have deep surfaces and vibrant neon/pastel accents for visual impact.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics! I\'ve determined the files that require modification: `theme.ts`, `ThemeIllustrations.tsx`, and `WritingCard.tsx`. I\'m updating the theme definitions to use SVG icons instead of emojis, adding high-contrast text tokens, and integrating distinctive styling props. I will then create theme-specific vector art with Gen Z flair, including Coquette bows, Y2K starbursts, and Matcha tea leaves. Finally, I will restyle the writing cards for bold contrast and thematic stamps.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
