  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Mode Switcher**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the dark/light mode switcher within `Navigation.tsx`. Specifically, I\'ve identified the need to switch the text from white to black for better visibility on the dark background. This adjustment is targeting lines 183-190 within the file.\n\n\n**Analyzing Mode Mismatch**\n\nI\'ve discovered the root cause of the black icon on the dark background. The OS media query activated `dark:bg-zinc-950`, but the React state held `mode` as \'light\', rendering a dark-gray moon. This mismatch is compounded by the button container having a `dark:bg-zinc-800` class. I\'m now implementing the user\'s request: switching to a white moon in light mode to resolve this visual issue.\n\n\n**Refining Icon Visibility**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the light mode switcher styling. My goal is to make the switcher button really pop. In light mode, I\'m thinking of a white moon icon with a dark pill-shaped background, and a white border. The user wants the text black in light mode. I\'m also ensuring that card colors stay consistent, regardless of the theme.\n\n\n**Improving Card Visibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on card design. The key is to maintain theme consistency: card backgrounds should utilize theme colors with a contrasting shade for readability. I\'m aiming for bold and dark theme emphasis for greater visibility. I\'ve been considering color matching, and I will be working on a GenZ-aesthetic friendly design, as requested.\n\n\n**Implementing Card Styling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the user\'s detailed card design request. I\'m moving away from random rainbow borders! The goal is now consistent theme-based styling, for example, for the \"Coquette Blush\" theme: The card background will be a shade of coquette blush, and the borders are bold coquette ribbon contours. Text will be jet black for high contrast, ensuring clarity, while metadata will be in dark text. No washed-out colors!\n\n\n**Defining Card Theme Consistency**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in theming the cards! I\'ve fleshed out specific designs for Cyber Y2K, Matcha Latte, and Midnight Muse themes. Cyber Y2K uses a crisp lavender/icy blue background with an electric indigo border and a chrome star badge. Matcha Latte gets a creamy matcha background with a forest green border and a matcha leaf badge. Midnight Muse features a lilac background with an obsidian violet border and a crescent moon badge. All themes use jet black text.\n\n\n**Adjusting Text Visibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on text visibility within `ThemeHeroIllustration.tsx`. I\'ve addressed the hard-to-read white text on a light pink background in screenshot 1. I\'m implementing deep contrast by making the banner text bold and using `text-rose-950` in light mode and `text-white` in dark mode. Also, I\'m ensuring all main headings and body prose use `text-black` in light mode.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_454714"
      name: "view_file"
