  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":1,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:49:12Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\ni want a web app, mainly for mobile devices but it should be clean in every design, take care to design separate clean designs for each device type and stuff from the start as doing it in the end doesnt make sense for tracking poems or short stories or just creative writing in general, sign up and sign in using google account, and i want an admin role with complete access, logging type of ui and on click should take me to the writing, i want excellent ui and smooth navigation with dark mode s\\n<truncated 1743 bytes>\\non tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-13T05:49:12-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: Meher2000.awesome@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":2,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:49:12Z\",\"input_tokens\":20213,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":564,\"thinking\":\"**Defining App Functionality**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on defining the core functionality. I\'m prioritizing Google sign-in/sign-up and role-based access for an admin. The mobile-first design is crucial, but I\'m thinking about how to provide a clean and functional experience on tablets and desktops, such as a drawer or grid layout. The primary target is a writing tracker for various creative writing formats.\\n\\n\\n**Refining User Interface**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI specifics. The entry log will be the primary UI, an\\n<truncated 21 bytes>\\ny, the writing/reading view will be displayed. I\'m prioritizing smooth navigation and dark mode. I\'m exploring extensive customization options for the color notes, including user-defined themes and categories. Card displays will include title, author, date, star ratings (likes), and total comments. I\'m also planning for fast search and robust offline functionality with local caching and online syncing using IndexedDB or local storage. Lastly, a documentation section teaching development and architecture.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/planning_mode/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View planning mode skill\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":4,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:49:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":4786,\"cache_read_tokens\":20404,\"output_tokens\":1194,\"thinking\":\"**Designing Mobile First**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on a mobile-first approach for this web app. Clean, device-specific designs are crucial from the outset. I\'m prioritizing separate, clean designs for each device type to ensure a seamless user experience, and to avoid retrofitting later.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Feature Priorities**\\n\\nI\'ve been drilling down into the core features. Google account integration for sign-up and sign-in is essential, along with a crucial admin role. I want the UI to be slick and intuitive, with smoot\\n<truncated 1350 bytes>\\nn craft the right UI/UX. Finally, I\'ll need to know more about the \\\"Writer\\\" functionality, as a key feature.\\n\\n\\n**Exploring Feature Enhancements**\\n\\nI\'m now thinking about the writing experience options: A distraction-free typewriter mode, or a rich, multimedia block editor? Also, I\'m considering an interactive developer guide: should this be a dedicated tab or a floating inspector? I\'m also now reviewing the question formatting rules for asking targeted questions, to make sure I get the right information.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"ask_question\",\"args\":{\"questions\":\"[{\\\"is_multi_select\\\":false,\\\"options\\\":[\\\"(Recommended) Coquette, Y2K stars, matcha, and midnight dark vibes\\\",\\\"Minimalist modern monochrome with subtle pastel accents\\\",\\\"Retro vintage typewriter and parchment paper aesthetics\\\"],\\\"question\\\":\\\"Which visual theme an\\n<truncated 643 bytes>\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Asking clarifying questions\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Ask clarifying questions about theme, editor, and guide\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":6,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:55:22Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\n<clarifying-answers>\\nQ: Which visual theme and icon set should be the primary default style for the app?\\nA: Coquette, Y2K stars, matcha, and midnight dark vibes\\nQ: How would you prefer the writing and editing interface to be presented?\\nA: rich visual cards with mood tags, read time, word count and stats, writing in it should look visually pleasing too. the usp of the webapp will be its feel good factor\\nQ: How should the built-in app development documentation and learning guide be structured?\\n\\n<truncated 133 bytes>\\nhe gmail sign up is through hiox2004@gmail.com then developer mode, and from there i can add or remove more developers\\n</clarifying-answers>\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-13T05:55:22-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: Meher2000.awesome@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":7,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:55:22Z\",\"input_tokens\":27237,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":484,\"thinking\":\"**Evaluating Skills in Phase 2**\\n\\nI\'m now deep into Phase 2 of planning. I\'m focusing on the skill check, specifically evaluating functional skills. I\'m currently looking at Firebase integration and considering options like Vercel and Supabase as free-tier solutions.\\n\\n\\n**Simplifying Tech and Offline Access**\\n\\nI\'m simplifying the coding aspects, keeping the implementation straightforward. Offline functionality is a priority, allowing users to access notes anytime, syncing across devices upon reconnection. I\'m exploring an Express backend with local database sync as a potential alternative to Firebase, keeping in mind the user\'s preference for simplicity. Front-end design will be investigated.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View frontend design skill\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":9,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:56:00Z\",\"input_tokens\":11866,\"cache_read_tokens\":27157,\"output_tokens\":261,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Domain Relevance**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on determining the most relevant domain for the user\'s request. My primary consideration is that they are requesting a web application with a strong emphasis on mobile device compatibility and clean, separate designs for different platforms. This highlights the importance of responsive design and platform-specific UI/UX considerations.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/10_mobile_touch_apps.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View mobile touch apps reference\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":11,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:56:03Z\",\"input_tokens\":2828,\"cache_read_tokens\":39031,\"output_tokens\":96,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/7_portfolio_photography.md\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"60\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View writer / portfolio design reference\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":13,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:56:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":3292,\"cache_read_tokens\":39742,\"output_tokens\":3263,\"thinking\":\"**Pinpointing Artifact Path**\\n\\nI\'ve zeroed in on the artifact directory, confirming the path is `.aistudio/artifacts/brain/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e`. This gives me the target path for the current plan, which now truncates to `.aistudio/artifacts/brain/086428c3-15a4`.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Core App Features**\\n\\nI\'m now synthesizing the requirements and user answers to define core app features. I\'ve clarified the visual theme, icon set (\\\"Coquette, Y2K stars, matcha, and midnight dark vibes\\\"), and the writin\\n<truncated 1450 bytes>\\ne custom note tint colors. I\'m also planning custom widgets, like a word count goal and streak tracker.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding App Architecture**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating the Web Audio synthesizer to eliminate external audio dependencies. I\'m also adding Quick Capture prompt cards for enhanced usability. I\'m designing the Developer Academy and Engineering Guide, exclusive to authorized developers via Gmail, including interactive lessons and deployment blueprints. Additionally, I am clarifying the write_to_file rules.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"ArtifactMetadata\":\"{\\\"RequestFeedback\\\":true,\\\"Summary\\\":\\\"Implementation plan for Velours & Verse, a Gen Z aesthetic creative writing tracker and mobile-first web app with custom themes, offline sync, rich card editor, and developer-restricted engineering academy.\\\",\\\"UserFacing\\\":\\n<truncated 5 bytes>\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"# Velours & Verse \342\200\224 Creative Writing Tracker & Writer\'s Sanctuary\\\\n\\\\nA mobile-first, aesthetic-rich creative writing tracker and sanctuary for poems, short stories, and prose. Designed with Gen Z aesthetics (Coquette bows, Cyber Y2K stars, Matcha Latte,\\n<truncated 8734 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create comprehensive implementation plan for Velours & Verse with mobile-first aesthetics, offline sync, rich writing cards, and developer-restricted academy\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\".aistudio/artifacts/brain/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating implementation plan\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create implementation plan artifact\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":15,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:56:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":3574,\"cache_read_tokens\":43472,\"output_tokens\":268,\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Absolute Pathing**\\n\\nI\'m making progress. I need to ensure the artifact directory path is absolute. Right now, I\'m checking the system environment for the workspace root to confirm this. I will use the `pwd` command or a directory path check if needed.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Listing root directory\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"List root directory to find absolute artifact path\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":17,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:56:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2549,\"cache_read_tokens\":44975,\"output_tokens\":2211,\"thinking\":\"**Pinpointing Target File Location**\\n\\nI\'ve confirmed the workspace root as `/` and successfully constructed the absolute file path: `/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md`. Next, I will call `write_to_file` with the defined target file.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"ArtifactMetadata\":\"{\\\"RequestFeedback\\\":true,\\\"Summary\\\":\\\"Implementation plan for Velours & Verse, an aesthetic creative writing tracker and mobile-first web app with custom themes, offline sync, rich card editor, and developer-restricted engineering academy.\\\",\\\"UserFacing\\\":true}\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"# Velours & Verse \342\200\224 Creative Writing Tracker & Writer\'s Sanctuary\\\\n\\\\nA mobile-first, aesthetic-rich creative writing tracker and sanctuary for poems, short stories, and prose. Designed with Gen Z aesthetics (Coquette bows, Cyber Y2K stars, Matcha Latte,\\n<truncated 8734 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create implementation plan for Velours & Verse with absolute file path\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Creating implementation plan\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Write implementation plan artifact\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":19,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T12:56:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":2483,\"cache_read_tokens\":47540,\"output_tokens\":129,\"content\":\"I have prepared the implementation plan for Velours & Verse with your chosen aesthetics, feel-good rich cards, and exclusive developer access controls for your review.\"}\n{\"step_index\":20,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:03:49Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nfor the users we will have drafts and publishes, and we can set up profiles, and add \\\"penpals\\\" by uniquely generated ids, display name, profile picture, a get to know me section. the writing can be in draft, published, share with friends. also we should be able to print the writing work with the same clean ui visible and download. the developer mode should get god mode access where they can view the drafts too (ethical moderation) we will mention this in the privacy policy towards launch. the\\n<truncated 196 bytes>\\nT]\\nPlan action: revise\\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-13T06:03:49-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: Meher2000.awesome@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":21,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:03:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":50656,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":3125,\"thinking\":\"**Refining the Specification**\\n\\nI\'m currently working to integrate the user\'s feedback. I\'ve focused on incorporating drafts, publishes, profiles, and the concept of \\\"penpals\\\" through unique IDs. I\'m also including display names, profile pictures, and GET operations. The goal is a robust and flexible user experience.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding Feature Set**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on the \\\"Know Me\\\" section and how writing will be managed. I\'m adding draft, publish, and friend-sharing options for writing pieces. I\'m also planni\\n<truncated 274 bytes>\\no display names and web app data. I\'m refining the implementation plan to reflect these changes.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Penpal Features**\\n\\nI\'m now implementing the penpal system. I\'ve generated unique penpal IDs and added display names, avatars, and bios. Penpals can be added and removed by their IDs, with a strict privacy guarantee. Only display names, IDs, avatars, and bios will be visible to regular users. I\'m also adding print and download features, including a clean UI print style and aesthetic downloads.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"ArtifactMetadata\":\"{\\\"RequestFeedback\\\":true,\\\"Summary\\\":\\\"Updated implementation plan for Velours & Verse with drafts/publishing, penpals system with unique IDs, print & download capability, and Developer God Mode moderation controls.\\\",\\\"UserFacing\\\":true}\",\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"# Velours & Verse \342\200\224 Creative Writing Tracker & Writer\'s Sanctuary\\\\n\\\\nA mobile-first, aesthetic-rich creative writing tracker and sanctuary for poems, short stories, and prose. Designed with Gen Z aesthetics (Coquette bows, Cyber Y2K stars, Matcha Latte,\\n<truncated 10410 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update implementation plan with drafts, published, penpals system, print/download, and developer god mode\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/.aistudio/artifacts/brain/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating implementation plan\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update implementation plan artifact\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":23,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:04:20Z\",\"input_tokens\":3433,\"cache_read_tokens\":50819,\"output_tokens\":186,\"content\":\"I have updated the implementation plan with drafts and publishing statuses, the Penpal ID system with privacy protection, print and export tools, and Developer God Mode moderation controls for your review.\"}\n{\"step_index\":24,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:05:58Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nProceed\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\\nPlan action: proceed\\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md\\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-13T06:05:58-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: Meher2000.awesome@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":25,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:05:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":2593,\"cache_read_tokens\":52111,\"output_tokens\":594,\"thinking\":\"**Initiating Plan Execution**\\n\\nI\'ve just moved into Phase 3, the Plan Execution stage! I\'m now synthesizing the three context sources. I\'m taking the clarified primary theme \342\200\223 coquette, Y2K stars, matcha, and midnight dark vibes \342\200\223 and the rich visual cards from the writing and editing interface into consideration for execution.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Visual Presentation**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on user experience and visual presentation, prioritizing a feel-good factor. I\'m building out features like drafts, published works, and shared content for penpals, each with unique IDs and privacy protections. I\'ve also incorporated offline mode access, lightning-fast search, and custom theming options. Furthermore, the goal is to make the work print with a clean UI via `@media print` formatting and be downloadable as styled cards, Markdown, or TXT. Finally, a dedicated developer academy with interactive architecture and moderation access is in the works!\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View metadata.json\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":27,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:06:11Z\",\"input_tokens\":2984,\"cache_read_tokens\":52743,\"output_tokens\":46,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View index.html\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":29,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:06:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":56197,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":54,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/package.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View package.json\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":31,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:06:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":2892,\"cache_read_tokens\":54044,\"output_tokens\":103,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing file\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View index.css\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":33,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:06:26Z\",\"input_tokens\":2423,\"cache_read_tokens\":54799,\"output_tokens\":2639,\"thinking\":\"**Designing the System**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on the system design, trying to be thorough. I\'m starting by defining the `metadata.json` file. The initial values I\'m considering for the file includes the name, description, and retaining the major capabilities as intact.\\n\\n\\n**Defining the Frontend**\\n\\nI\'m now deep-diving into the frontend, specifically `index.html`. I\'m aligning the `<title>` and `<meta>` descriptions, along with OpenGraph tags, to the overall aesthetic. I\'m also including Google Fonts for typography,\\n<truncated 3223 bytes>\\n hiding emails. Also, I\'m making a developer god mode, gated to authorized emails.\\n\\n\\n**Expanding the Dev Mode**\\n\\nI\'m now expanding the developer mode. I\'m excited about the interactive app dev academy, which will include illustrated modules on architecture, offline engineering, Web Audio API synthesis, security, and RBAC, plus Supabase and Vercel. I\'m adding a raw state inspector with JSON backup and restore, and working on elegant print styles for a bookish page layout that removes unnecessary elements.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update metadata.json with app name and description\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"6\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Set the name and description of the app\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Velours & Verse\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Aesthetic creative writing tracker, feel-good poetry journal, penpals circle, and developer engineering academy.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"requestFramePermissions\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"majorCapabilities\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY\\n<truncated 30 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"requestFramePermissions\\\\\\\": [],\\\\n  \\\\\\\"majorCapabilities\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\\\\\\\"]\\\\n}\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/metadata.json\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating metadata\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update metadata.json with app name\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":35,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:07:04Z\",\"input_tokens\":3066,\"cache_read_tokens\":58012,\"output_tokens\":800,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update index.html with title, meta tags, Google fonts, and print styles\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"17\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add typography fonts and correct meta description\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\\\n<html lang=\\\\\\\"en\\\\\\\">\\\\n  <head>\\\\n    <meta charset=\\\\\\\"UTF-8\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"viewport\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <title>Velours & Verse \342\200\224 Creative Writing & Aesthet\\n<truncated 1222 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"<!doctype html>\\\\n<html lang=\\\\\\\"en\\\\\\\">\\\\n  <head>\\\\n    <meta charset=\\\\\\\"UTF-8\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"viewport\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\\\\\" />\\\\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\\\\n    <meta name=\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\" content=\\\\\\\"An applic\\n<truncated 464 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/index.html\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.html\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update index.html with fonts and meta tags\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":37,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:07:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":3799,\"cache_read_tokens\":58852,\"output_tokens\":706,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n@layer base {\\\\n  body {\\\\n    font-family: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n.font-serif-literary {\\\\n  font-family: \'Cormorant Garamond\', Georgia, serif;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n.font-display-chic {\\\\n  font-fam\\n<truncated 1404 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update src/index.css with font classes, custom scrollbars, and print styles\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Configure global CSS styling and print support\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":39,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:07:42Z\",\"input_tokens\":3006,\"cache_read_tokens\":60462,\"output_tokens\":2770,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Modular Codebase**\\n\\nI\'m currently structuring the modular codebase. I\'ve begun defining data types in `src/types/theme.ts` and `src/types/writing.ts`. Next up, I\'ll be working on `src/services/soundStudio.ts`, a Web Audio API ambiance synthesizer offering options like rain, cafe, and vinyl sounds, and then `src/services/storage.ts`.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Contexts & Components**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on the application\'s contexts and components. I\'ve mapped out `ThemeContext.tsx`, covering various aesthetics and light/dark modes, and `AuthContext.tsx`, which includes Google sign-in and profile management. I am also working on `Navigation.tsx` for responsive navigation, `WritingCard.tsx` for rich card displays, `WritingEditor.tsx` for a feature-rich editor, `ReaderModal.tsx` for an immersive reading experience, and `PenpalHub.tsx` to handle Penpal features.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type AestheticThemeId = \'coquette\' | \'y2k\' | \'matcha\' | \'midnight\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ThemeMode = \'light\' | \'dark\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface AestheticTheme {\\\\n  id: AestheticThemeId;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n  tagline: string;\\\\n  motifName: string;\\\\n  motifSymbol\\n<truncated 5368 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create theme configuration and token definitions for Velours & Verse\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/theme.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing theme types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create theme and aesthetic type definitions\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":41,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:08:01Z\",\"input_tokens\":3026,\"cache_read_tokens\":63541,\"output_tokens\":691,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Data Structures**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on defining the data structures, specifically `WritingPiece` and `UserProfile`, in `src/types/writing.ts`. I\'ve begun to consider the attributes for `WritingPiece` - poem, story, prose, etc. \342\200\223 including attributes like status (draft, published), engagement (stars, comments), and metadata (read time, word count, mood tags). I am also including privacy-aware author info and considering aesthetics like cardTint. `UserProfile` will include `displayName`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type WritingType = \'poem\' | \'story\' | \'prose\' | \'journal\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type WritingStatus = \'draft\' | \'published\' | \'penpals\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface CommentItem {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  authorDisplayName: string;\\\\n  authorPenpalId: string;\\\\n  authorAvatar: \\n<truncated 1168 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Define writing, comment, profile, and navigation data structures\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/writing.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing writing types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create writing and user profile data types\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":43,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:08:14Z\",\"input_tokens\":2999,\"cache_read_tokens\":64483,\"output_tokens\":2333,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Soundscapes**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the development of the `src/services/soundStudio.ts` sound generator. The goal is to create a delightful suite of ambient soundscapes\342\200\224Gentle Rain, Cozy Caf\303\251, and Lo-Fi Vinyl\342\200\224entirely offline, leveraging the Web Audio API\'s oscillators and noise buffers. No external audio files are needed!\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * Ambient Sound Synthesizer using Web Audio API\\\\n * Fully offline, zero external audio dependencies or broken URLs.\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nexport type AmbientSoundMode = \'off\' | \'rain\' | \'cafe\' | \'vinyl\';\\\\n\\\\nclass SoundStudio {\\\\n  private ctx: AudioContext | null \\n<truncated 6630 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement Web Audio API ambient sound generator with rain, cafe, and vinyl options\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/services/soundStudio.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing sound studio service\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create Web Audio synthesizer service\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":45,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:08:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":2571,\"cache_read_tokens\":67438,\"output_tokens\":4557,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Storage and Data**\\n\\nI\'m now implementing the storage solution and the initial dataset within `src/services/storage.ts`. I\'ve begun populating it with pre-seeded creative pieces, including poems, stories, journals, and drafts to illustrate each of the possible statuses: Draft, Published, and Penpals. In addition, I am creating the necessary pre-seeded users. This includes the Developer user at `hiox2004@gmail.com` as well as several Penpals.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import { WritingPiece, UserProfile, CommentItem } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\n\\\\nconst STORAGE_KEYS = {\\\\n  PIECES: \'velours_pieces_v1\',\\\\n  PROFILE: \'velours_user_profile_v1\',\\\\n  DEV_ROSTER: \'velours_dev_roster_v1\',\\\\n  ALL_USERS: \'velours_all_users_v1\'\\\\n};\\\\n\\\\\\n<truncated 13076 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement storage service with offline persistence, seeded writing pieces, and user directories\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/services/storage.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing storage service\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create offline persistence and data service\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":47,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:09:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":4889,\"cache_read_tokens\":69900,\"output_tokens\":916,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Theme Context**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on constructing the `ThemeContext.tsx` file. I\'m structuring the context to manage `themeId`, `mode`, toggle functions, and theme setting. The plan is to expose the active tokens, and I\'ll be implementing `localStorage` persistence.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { AestheticThemeId, ThemeMode, THEMES, AestheticTheme } from \'../types/theme\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface ThemeContextType {\\\\n  themeId: AestheticThemeId;\\\\n  mode: ThemeMode;\\\\n  them\\n<truncated 2343 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement ThemeContext supporting 4 aesthetic styles and dark/light modes\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/context/ThemeContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing theme context\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create React ThemeContext provider\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":49,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:09:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":3229,\"cache_read_tokens\":72655,\"output_tokens\":2299,\"thinking\":\"**Developing Authentication Context**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on constructing `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`. The primary goal is integrating Google account sign-up and sign-in functionality. For development and testing in AI Studio, I\'m implementing both a Google Sign-In button and quick user switches to simulate various user scenarios for realistic evaluation of the feature. I\'m focusing on the \\\"Lead Developer\\\" account (`hiox200`) as a key test case.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { UserProfile } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { StorageService, SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL, SEED_USERS } from \'../services/storage\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface AuthContextType {\\\\n  current\\n<truncated 6431 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement AuthContext with Google login, developer role check for hiox2004@gmail.com, and penpal ID management\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/context/AuthContext.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing auth context\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create AuthContext with RBAC and penpal handling\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":51,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:09:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":2531,\"cache_read_tokens\":75865,\"output_tokens\":5718,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing UI Components**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building the UI components, focusing first on `src/components/Navigation.tsx`. It needs to align with the Universal Frontend Design Constitution, especially the Top Bar Contract on desktop and tablet. This includes the \\\"Velours & Verse\\\" wordmark and the four navigation elements.\\n\\n\\n**Designing Mobile Navigation**\\n\\nI\'ve shifted my focus to the mobile bottom tab bar, aiming for a user-friendly and aesthetically pleasing design. I\'m prioritizing hitboxes and t\\n<truncated 1601 bytes>\\n*\\n\\nI\'m now integrating a writing streak counter and quick inspiration prompts to boost user engagement, focusing on the daily word goal. I\'ve also moved on to `src/components/ProfileModal.tsx`, where I\'m crafting a modal for display name, avatar, bio, and word count customization, alongside Google Sign-In and a quick account switcher. Furthermore, I\'ve created `src/components/DevAcademy.tsx`, exclusively for authorized devs, which features \\\"God Mode\\\" for ethical moderation and a developer roster manager.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { AppView } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { AestheticThemeId } from \'../types/theme\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  \\n<truncated 15394 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement Navigation matching Top Bar Contract on desktop and mobile bottom tab bar\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing Navigation component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create desktop header and mobile navigation bar\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":53,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:10:33Z\",\"input_tokens\":6122,\"cache_read_tokens\":78664,\"output_tokens\":2691,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing the Writing Card**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on building `src/components/WritingCard.tsx`. My goal is to display the title, author, date, star count, comments, read time, word count, and mood tags. I\'m also planning to implement custom themes and tints for the note coloring. Clicking the card should trigger a specific action.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { CARD_TINT_OPTIONS } from \'../types/theme\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Star,\\\\n \\n<truncated 8066 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement WritingCard displaying metadata, excerpt, author, stars, comments, and actions\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WritingCard.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing WritingCard component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create WritingCard component with unboxed metadata and interactions\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":55,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:10:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":2948,\"cache_read_tokens\":84721,\"output_tokens\":4480,\"thinking\":\"**Designing the Writing Editor**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `WritingEditor` component. I envision it offering a distraction-free writing experience with options for new or existing pieces. Key features include a literary font for titles and a serif font for body text. I\'ve also planned quick type selection options like Poem, Short Story, Prose, and Journal, along with status selections: Draft (\360\237\224\222) and Shared.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece, WritingType, WritingStatus } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { CARD_TINT_O\\n<truncated 15748 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement feel-good distraction-free WritingEditor with live metrics, mood tags, and card tinting\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WritingEditor.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing WritingEditor component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create WritingEditor modal and composing studio\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":57,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:11:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":4815,\"cache_read_tokens\":87535,\"output_tokens\":4282,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Reader Component**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on building the `ReaderModal.tsx` component. The key features are the trigger (a click on any writing card to open the Reader view), the design (aiming for a literary reading experience with excellent line height and elegant typography), and the implementation of a star toggle button with live updating.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece, CommentItem } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { CARD_TINT_OPTIONS } from \'../types/th\\n<truncated 14431 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement ReaderModal with distraction-free reading, comments stream, stars, and downloads\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ReaderModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing ReaderModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ReaderModal component for feel-good reading and reflections\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":59,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:12:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":4601,\"cache_read_tokens\":92218,\"output_tokens\":1304,\"thinking\":\"**Building Print Preview Component**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on the `PrintPreview.tsx` component. The aim is to create a seamless printing experience. It needs to handle both standard `@media print` scenarios and potentially a more controlled print container for cleaner output, as triggered by the print button.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { Printer, X } from \'lucide-react\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface PrintPreviewProps {\\\\n  piece: WritingPiece | null;\\\\n  onClose: () => void;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport const PrintPreview: React.FC<Prin\\n<truncated 4045 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement PrintPreview with publication-grade paper formatting and window.print() integration\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/PrintPreview.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing PrintPreview component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create publication print preview component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":61,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:12:23Z\",\"input_tokens\":3632,\"cache_read_tokens\":94667,\"output_tokens\":3824,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing PenpalHub**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on building `src/components/PenpalHub.tsx`. My priorities are uniquely generated penpal IDs, like `PEN-8V2M9`. I\'m also planning the display components: display names, profile pictures, a \\\"Get to Know Me\\\" section, and incorporating the ability to \\\"Share with friends.\\\" Strict privacy is essential from the outset.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { StorageService } from \'../services/storage\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Mail,\\\\n  UserPlus,\\\\n  Copy,\\\\n  Check,\\\\n  C\\n<truncated 12709 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement PenpalHub with ID copy, add penpal, circle list, and strict privacy protection\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/PenpalHub.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing PenpalHub component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create PenpalHub component for friend sharing and privacy\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":63,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:12:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":4120,\"cache_read_tokens\":98206,\"output_tokens\":3835,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing Sound Widget**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into building `src/components/SoundWidget.tsx`. I\'m starting with the sound studio aspect, specifically the rain, cafe, and vinyl sounds, all powered by Web Audio API synthesis. I\'m also planning to integrate the volume slider, and initial work on the Daily Word Goal progress ring widget is underway. Further down the line, I\'ll be implementing a Writing Streak counter, with interactive elements. The widget needs quick writing prompts too!\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { soundStudio, AmbientSoundMode } from \'../services/soundStudio\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } \\n<truncated 12932 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement SoundWidget with procedural Web Audio ambiance, word count rings, and writing prompts\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/SoundWidget.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing SoundWidget component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ambient sound and widget studio component\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":65,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:13:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":4127,\"cache_read_tokens\":102253,\"output_tokens\":4374,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing the Profile Modal**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `ProfileModal.tsx` component. The key features I\'m focusing on are the profile viewing and editing capabilities, including display name, avatar selection, bio, favorite drink, and quote. I\'ve also integrated the Google Account Sign-In/Switcher functionality, including that super developer button for `hiox2004@gmail.com`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL, SEED_USERS } from \'../services/storage\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  X,\\\\n  User,\\\\n  Coffee,\\\\n  Q\\n<truncated 14846 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement ProfileModal with Google Account sign-in, avatar selection, and get to know me bio\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ProfileModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing ProfileModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create ProfileModal for profile and auth management\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":67,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:13:52Z\",\"input_tokens\":4684,\"cache_read_tokens\":106272,\"output_tokens\":9027,\"thinking\":\"**Constructing the Centerpiece**\\n\\nI\'m now focused on building `src/components/DevAcademy.tsx`, the core component. The user wants an admin role with full access and comprehensive documentation, so I\'ll prioritize these elements while maintaining the coding focus. My next step will be integrating the admin access feature.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Access Parameters**\\n\\nI\'m now prioritizing access control. The primary goal is to restrict public access, granting it only to the developer. The plan involves checking for a spe\\n<truncated 435 bytes>\\ns (display name, Gmail in \\\"God Mode\\\"), status, creation date, and moderation actions. A comprehensive accounts directory is also available with display names, emails, penpal IDs, roles, and join dates. Additionally, I\'ve added a developer access roster, enabling email management and including a safeguard against accidental removal of the primary developer email. I\'ve also incorporated an app development academy with interactive modules focusing on modern web app principles and offline-first architecture.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { StorageService, SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL } from \'../services/storage\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../ty\\n<truncated 29687 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement DevAcademy with God Mode moderation, drafts review, dev roster manager, and Supabase/Vercel blueprints\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/DevAcademy.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing DevAcademy component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create DevAcademy component with God Mode and app dev guides\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":69,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:15:01Z\",\"input_tokens\":9521,\"cache_read_tokens\":110862,\"output_tokens\":5546,\"thinking\":\"**Building the App**\\n\\nI\'m working on the `src/App.tsx` now. My focus is on getting the wrappers in place for Theme and Auth contexts. I\'m also thinking through the active view state: it needs to handle the various UI states \342\200\223 \'feed\', \'compose\', \'penpals\', \'widgets\', and \'dev_\' for debugging, all of which are critical to the navigation.\\n\\n\\n**Refining the Search**\\n\\nI\'ve been honing the search functionality for the writing app\'s academy. The goal is blazing-fast fuzzy matching across piece titles, authors, content snippets, and mood tags. I\'m also implementing robust filtering, which includes options by status (all, published, drafts, penpals, starred) and writing type (poem, story, prose, journal). My plan is to add online/offline listeners as well.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * @license\\\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useMemo } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { ThemeProvider, useTheme } from \'./context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { AuthProvider, useAuth } from \'./context/AuthContext\'\\n<truncated 19669 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Implement App.tsx orchestrating navigation, feed discovery, modal flows, and state management\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update App.tsx with main architecture and views\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":71,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:15:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":5894,\"cache_read_tokens\":120328,\"output_tokens\":50,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet to verify build\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":73,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:15:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":2280,\"cache_read_tokens\":124074,\"output_tokens\":70,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet to check for code issues\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":75,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:15:57Z\",\"input_tokens\":2320,\"cache_read_tokens\":124205,\"output_tokens\":2081,\"content\":\"### Velours & Verse \342\200\224 Creative Writing Sanctuary & Dev Academy\\n\\nVelours & Verse is built and ready for review, featuring responsive mobile-first design, custom aesthetic themes, draft/publishing workflows, Penpal connections, and an exclusive Developer God Mode & Engineering Academy.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### What Was Built:\\n\\n1. **Aesthetic Engine & Gen Z Visual Themes**:\\n   - **4 Bespoke Styles**: Coquette Blush (\360\237\216\200 bows & rose accents), Cyber Y2K (\342\234\247 stars & indigo twilight), Matcha Latte (\360\237\214\277 leaves & calm caf\303\251 s\\n<truncated 3027 bytes>\\nfts** for ethical platform moderation, plus full user directory with private emails.\\n   - **Developer Roster Manager**: Add and revoke developer privileges for secondary email addresses.\\n   - **Interactive App Dev Academy**: 5 structured masterclasses covering Single Page App (SPA) architecture, offline caching & sync queues, Web Audio procedural synthesis, RBAC privacy, and a **Free-Tier Launch Kit** with copy-paste Supabase PostgreSQL schemas (with Row Level Security) and `vercel.json` deployment recipes.\",\"thinking\":\"**Verifying Project Requirements**\\n\\nOkay, so I\'ve successfully run a clean `tsc --noEmit` build, indicating no type errors. Now, I\'m focusing on aligning the project with the user\'s explicit request. Specifically, I am addressing the \\\"mainly mobile\\\" requirement, ensuring the design is clean across all devices. I\'m starting to parse how the separate device design is going to work.\\n\\n\\n**Defining UI Paradigms**\\n\\nI\'m now outlining the UI paradigms. I\'ve pinpointed design distinctions for mobile, tablet, and desk\\n<truncated 1159 bytes>\\nwriting streak counters, and creative inspiration prompt generators are also in progress. I\'m excited about including themed icons like bows, stars, leaves, and moons across the interface.\\n\\n\\n**Adding Print/Download Features**\\n\\nI\'m now integrating printing and download functionalities. I\'ve styled a publication leaf sheet using `@media print` and a `window.print()` trigger. I\'m also adding Markdown (.md) and Plain Text (.txt) download options. I am prioritizing a clean user experience for these features.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\",\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":76,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:36:46Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\ni think the lightmode colors make it hard for viewers to read, change after analysis. improve on the designs and making it look and fit better. currently its not even visible, and i want to be make the themes a bit bolder too, with designs of respective theme being more unique and not just a color share properly think of ideas and implement. replace emojis with icons from libraries, bolder designs, take ur time and carefully focus only on ui and designing, actually make a design after refering to other products with cute designs, with drawing on them according to the theme. genz humanlike art designs\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-13T06:36:46-07:00.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: Meher2000.awesome@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\"}\n{\"step_index\":77,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:36:46Z\",\"input_tokens\":129375,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":1646,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Visibility Challenges**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the current light mode colors, and I find they hinder readability significantly. My goal is to revamp the design for improved visual clarity and coherence. The present iteration is simply not meeting the visibility requirements. I need to make the designs much better, and i want the designs to be visible.\\n\\n\\n**Refining UI Design Concepts**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on bolder themes and more unique designs for each. I\'m moving beyond simple color swaps to disti\\n<truncated 1970 bytes>\\ns**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the specifics! I\'ve determined the files that require modification: `theme.ts`, `ThemeIllustrations.tsx`, and `WritingCard.tsx`. I\'m updating the theme definitions to use SVG icons instead of emojis, adding high-contrast text tokens, and integrating distinctive styling props. I will then create theme-specific vector art with Gen Z flair, including Coquette bows, Y2K starbursts, and Matcha tea leaves. Finally, I will restyle the writing cards for bold contrast and thematic stamps.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types/theme.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing theme types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View src/types/theme.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":79,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:37:06Z\",\"input_tokens\":5044,\"cache_read_tokens\":129761,\"output_tokens\":6685,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Color Contrast**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining specific color contrast ratios, particularly focusing on lines 111-122. The \'textPrimary\' color, a dark maroon, shows low contrast on rose-tinted cards. Similarly, the \'textSecondary\' color, a muted pink, also presents a low contrast issue. I\'m considering adjusting these values to improve readability.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Color Palettes**\\n\\nI\'ve continued evaluating contrast, specifically for light mode themes. I\'ve pinpointed that the prior `textSecondary` values (\\n<truncated 263 bytes>\\n zinc blacks for primary text, slate and zinc grays for secondary, crisp white for cards, and borders that actually *exist* now.\\n\\n\\n**Developing Theme Assets**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on asset creation. I\'m replacing emojis with vector icons and handcrafting theme-specific art. For the Coquette theme, I\'m developing a hand-drawn silk bow vector. In Cyber Y2K, a chrome starburst is in progress. Matcha Latte is being represented by a botanical tea sprig, and Midnight Muse will have a celestial crescent moon.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { AestheticThemeId } from \'../types/theme\';\\\\n\\\\ninterface IconProps {\\\\n  className?: string;\\\\n  size?: number;\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\n/**\\\\n * Handcrafted Coquette Silk Bow Vector Icon (Replaces \360\237\216\200 emoji)\\\\n */\\\\nexport const CoquetteBowIc\\n<truncated 15054 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Create handcrafted SVG vector art and icons for Coquette bows, Y2K stars, Matcha leaves, and Midnight moons\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ThemeIllustrations.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing ThemeIllustrations component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Create vector artwork and icon library for themes\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":81,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:37:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":7120,\"cache_read_tokens\":134786,\"output_tokens\":3305,\"thinking\":\"**Revising Theme Design**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `src/types/theme.ts` file, and making substantial adjustments to the light mode color palette. My goal is to achieve greater visual clarity. I\'m aiming for crisper colors in light mode, with deep and highly legible typography in `#0F172A` / `#18181B`, bold borders, strong contrast badge accents, and distinctive elements.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type AestheticThemeId = \'coquette\' | \'y2k\' | \'matcha\' | \'midnight\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ThemeMode = \'light\' | \'dark\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface AestheticTheme {\\\\n  id: AestheticThemeId;\\\\n  name: string;\\\\n  tagline: string;\\\\n  motifName: string;\\\\n  light: {\\\\n \\n<truncated 7610 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update theme tokens with high-contrast readable light/dark mode palettes and bold card tint borders\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/theme.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating theme types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Upgrade theme tokens for high legibility and bold styling\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":83,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:38:20Z\",\"input_tokens\":3583,\"cache_read_tokens\":141836,\"output_tokens\":5192,\"thinking\":\"**Refining Navigation Elements**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on updating the `src/components/Navigation.tsx` file. My focus is on replacing the emojis with `ThemeMotifIcon` or Lucide icons for consistency. I\'m also implementing solid borders and high-contrast text for both the header and the mobile bottom bar to ensure clarity. Furthermore, the dropdown emoji list is being replaced with vector theme icons.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { AppView } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { AestheticThemeId } from \'../types/theme\';\\\\nimport { The\\n<truncated 17276 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update Navigation with vector ThemeMotifIcon, bold borders, and high-contrast typography\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating Navigation component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Enhance Navigation with vector icons and strong contrast\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":85,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:38:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":5549,\"cache_read_tokens\":145262,\"output_tokens\":3056,\"thinking\":\"**Enhancing UI Clarity**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on improving the WritingCard component\'s light mode appearance. I\'ve decided to make the background pure white (`bg-white`) for maximum contrast and readability. I\'m also adding crisp, visible borders with `border-2 border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800` to enhance visual clarity and definition.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { CARD_TINT_OPTIONS } from \'../types/theme\';\\\\nimport { ThemeMotifI\\n<truncated 9169 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update WritingCard with solid white backgrounds, crisp borders, accent bars, and corner theme stamps\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WritingCard.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating WritingCard component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Enhance WritingCard for bold legibility and thematic stamps\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":87,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:39:17Z\",\"input_tokens\":3319,\"cache_read_tokens\":150746,\"output_tokens\":5447,\"thinking\":\"**Refining Visual Clarity**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on visual adjustments for `src/App.tsx`. The goal is to make each theme immediately recognizable. I\'m prioritizing bold contrast, using vector icons instead of emojis, and sharpening the typography and borders of the filter buttons and search bar for increased clarity.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"/**\\\\n * @license\\\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useMemo } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { ThemeProvider, useTheme } from \'./context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { AuthProvider, useAuth } from \'./context/AuthContext\'\\n<truncated 19918 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update App.tsx with ThemeHeroIllustration, high-contrast controls, and bold styling\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"