ith vector icons and Lucide icons to align better with the theme. Finally, I\'m opting for a solid white/slate background to sharpen the overall presentation.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { CARD_TINT_OPTIONS } from \'../types/theme\';\\\\nimport\\n<truncated 15594 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update ReaderModal with high contrast typography and clean vector motif accents\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ReaderModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing ReaderModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Enhance ReaderModal for bold readability and clean styling\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":93,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:40:51Z\",\"input_tokens\":4993,\"cache_read_tokens\":164552,\"output_tokens\":4048,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { StorageService } from \'../services/storage\';\\\\nimport { ThemeMotifIcon } from \'./ThemeIllustrations\';\\n<truncated 13360 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update PenpalHub with vector motifs, solid white cards, and high contrast typography\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/PenpalHub.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing PenpalHub component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Enhance PenpalHub for bold readability and clean vectors\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":95,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:41:27Z\",\"input_tokens\":4339,\"cache_read_tokens\":169369,\"output_tokens\":4094,\"thinking\":\"**Refining Visual Aesthetics**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the `SoundWidget` component, aiming for a more polished visual style. I\'m upgrading the typography to high contrast and incorporating clean vector art. I\'m also planning to replace emojis with Lucide icons. Finally, I\'m working to ensure the cards have a solid white background, crisp borders, and high-contrast text color.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState, useEffect } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { soundStudio, AmbientSoundMode } from \'../services/soundStudio\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } \\n<truncated 13509 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update SoundWidget with high contrast cards, vector motifs, and clean styling\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/SoundWidget.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing SoundWidget component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Enhance SoundWidget for bold readability and clean vectors\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":97,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:41:54Z\",\"input_tokens\":4383,\"cache_read_tokens\":173616,\"output_tokens\":4559,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL, SEED_USERS } from \'../services/storage\';\\\\nimport { ThemeMotifIcon } from \'./Theme\\n<truncated 15543 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update ProfileModal with high contrast styles and vector motifs\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ProfileModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing ProfileModal component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Enhance ProfileModal for bold readability and clean vectors\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":99,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:42:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":4861,\"cache_read_tokens\":177811,\"output_tokens\":8666,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { StorageService, SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL } from \'../services/storage\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../ty\\n<truncated 30570 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update DevAcademy with high-contrast text, bold borders, and vector theme motifs\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/DevAcademy.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing DevAcademy component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Enhance DevAcademy for bold readability and clean vectors\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":101,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:43:09Z\",\"input_tokens\":9108,\"cache_read_tokens\":182344,\"output_tokens\":68,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Compile applet to verify build\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":103,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:43:15Z\",\"input_tokens\":2290,\"cache_read_tokens\":189312,\"output_tokens\":42,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"lint_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Linting applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Lint applet code\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":105,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:43:20Z\",\"input_tokens\":2283,\"cache_read_tokens\":189462,\"output_tokens\":1131,\"content\":\"I have redesigned the visual architecture and theme system to resolve the legibility issues and deliver a bolder, distinctive aesthetic:\\n\\n### What Was Improved:\\n\\n1. **High-Contrast, Readable Light Mode (WCAG AAA)**:\\n   - **Razor-Sharp Typography**: Replaced low-contrast muted tones with deep `#18181B` / `#0F172A` headings and `#334155` body text for effortless daylight readability.\\n   - **Solid Surface Presence**: Writing cards now feature pure, crisp white surfaces with bold 2px borders (`border-zinc-300 d\\n<truncated 1100 bytes>\\n.\\n     - **Matcha Latte**: Ceramic latte cup with steaming aroma curves and botanical tea sprigs.\\n     - **Midnight Muse**: Hand-drawn crescent moon with celestial orbit stars and constellation lines.\\n   - Writing cards now feature subtle theme watermark stamps in the top corner for added tactile personality.\\n\\n4. **Bolder Controls & Touch Ergonomics**:\\n   - Search bar, filter segmented tabs, format buttons, and bottom tab navigation now feature bold 2px borders, tactile active states, and crisp icon labels.\",\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Visual Updates**\\n\\nI\'m pleased to report that the applet\'s code compiles and lints cleanly. Now I\'m carefully reviewing the recent visual updates. My focus is on improving the light mode\'s readability and overall design, ensuring the applet is clear and visually accessible, addressing the user\'s concerns about visibility. The key is in refining the design to create a more effective user experience.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Theming Details**\\n\\nI\'ve significantly revamped the visual themes. I\'ve abandoned the washed-out backgrounds and low-contrast text in favor of stark, high-contrast typography, achieving WCAG AAA readability. The white card surfaces now have bold borders and subtle drop shadows. Each theme boasts distinctive hand-crafted vector art, such as silk ribbon bows for the \\\"Coquette Blush Atelier\\\" theme, and chrome starburst constellations for \\\"Cyber Y2K Cyber Twilight.\\\"\\n\\n\\n\",\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":106,\"source\":\"USER_EXPLICIT\",\"type\":\"USER_INPUT\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:51:58Z\",\"content\":\"<USER_REQUEST>\\nokay so cant see black icon on black bg, change the text to white moon when in light mode. for the dark/light mode switcher\\n\\n- also in lightmode we have text in grey? we cant see make the color of text black, and also dont make the color of cards switch, keep it consistent with the theme, the cards should have the themes color and a shade of it as the bg for the card, but think about color matching and visibility of the colors. i added the screenshots of light mode, change color of text to ma\\n<truncated 325 bytes>\\ned\\n</USER_REQUEST>\\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-13T06:51:58-07:00.\\n\\nThe user has uploaded 2 image(s):\\n- image.png\\n- image.png\\nYou can embed these images in an artifact if you need the USER to review them.\\n\\nModel: models/gemini-3.8-flash\\nDevelopment App URL: https://ais-dev-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nShared App URL: https://ais-pre-6ma57ipuaf3mc7mbayx2pf-3063132358.asia-southeast1.run.app\\nUser Email: Meher2000.awesome@gmail.com\\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\",\"media\":[{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"image.png\"},{\"mime_type\":\"image/png\",\"uri\":\"image.png\"}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"content\"]}\n{\"step_index\":107,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:51:59Z\",\"input_tokens\":195649,\"cache_read_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":2035,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Feedback**\\n\\nI\'m meticulously reviewing the screenshots and the user\'s feedback, focusing intently on visual inconsistencies. Specifically, I\'ve noted the conflicting color modes: a dark top header against a light content area. This is a critical observation, a possible interface flaw.\\n\\n\\n**Investigating Dark Mode Bug**\\n\\nI\'ve got a major lead! The \\\"Writing Log & Discovery\\\" text is invisible on the white background. I believe I\'ve pinpointed the issue. The browser, or rather, the CSS, thinks we\\n<truncated 1674 bytes>\\nheme, not switch unexpectedly.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Card Styles**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on card design improvements. The user wants the card backgrounds to be consistent with the current theme, using the theme\'s color palette, a darker shade for visibility and color matching. In light mode, I\'ll go bolder and darker with the text, using matching lighter shades for backgrounds. I want to ensure readability and visual harmony, and making a bold, theme-focused design. I\'m focusing on Coquette colors for the example.\\n\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check index.css for dark mode variant\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":109,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:52:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":3178,\"cache_read_tokens\":196131,\"output_tokens\":349,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Dark Mode Effects**\\n\\nI\'ve discovered that `src/index.css` simply imports Tailwind CSS. This, combined with Tailwind CSS v4\'s default dark mode behavior via `@import`, suggests the application automatically applies `.dark:*` styles because my OS/browser is in dark mode, as evidenced by the screenshot.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add custom-variant dark for class-based dark mode in Tailwind v4\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"2\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Configure class-based dark mode in Tailwind CSS v4\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\\n\\\\n@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *));\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"@import \\\\\\\"tailwindcss\\\\\\\";\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/index.css\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating index.css\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Configure Tailwind CSS v4 dark mode variant\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":111,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:52:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2767,\"cache_read_tokens\":197213,\"output_tokens\":2274,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Mode Switcher**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the dark/light mode switcher within `Navigation.tsx`. Specifically, I\'ve identified the need to switch the text from white to black for better visibility on the dark background. This adjustment is targeting lines 183-190 within the file.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Mode Mismatch**\\n\\nI\'ve discovered the root cause of the black icon on the dark background. The OS media query activated `dark:bg-zinc-950`, but the React state held `mode` as \'light\', rendering a dark-gray moon\\n<truncated 1805 bytes>\\n background with an obsidian violet border and a crescent moon badge. All themes use jet black text.\\n\\n\\n**Adjusting Text Visibility**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on text visibility within `ThemeHeroIllustration.tsx`. I\'ve addressed the hard-to-read white text on a light pink background in screenshot 1. I\'m implementing deep contrast by making the banner text bold and using `text-rose-950` in light mode and `text-white` in dark mode. Also, I\'m ensuring all main headings and body prose use `text-black` in light mode.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types/theme.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing theme types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect current theme definitions\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":113,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:53:01Z\",\"input_tokens\":6750,\"cache_read_tokens\":200354,\"output_tokens\":3960,\"thinking\":\"**Adjusting for Clarity**\\n\\nI\'ve been reviewing the user\'s feedback concerning the interface\'s color scheme. The primary issue seems to be contrast, particularly the visibility of icons and text against backgrounds. I\'m focusing on making the \\\"moon\\\" icon white in light mode and switching the text to black in light mode. I\'m also ensuring that card colors remain constant. My objective is to create clear visual separation.\\n\\n\\n**Optimizing Color Schemes**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the color palette for both light a\\n<truncated 1190 bytes>\\n border, and pure black text to ensure high visibility.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Theme Specifics**\\n\\nI\'m now implementing theme-specific styles for Matcha Latte and Midnight Muse. For Matcha, I\'m using a creamy foam background, a deep forest border, pure black text, a forest matcha header accent, and a Matcha Leaf stamp. Midnight Muse features a lilac mist background, midnight purple border, black text, a deep violet accent, and a Crescent Moon stamp. Dark mode will use deep velvet backgrounds and bright borders.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"export type AestheticThemeId = \'coquette\' | \'y2k\' | \'matcha\' | \'midnight\';\\\\n\\\\nexport type ThemeMode = \'light\' | \'dark\';\\\\n\\\\nexport interface ThemeCardStyle {\\\\n  bg: string;\\\\n  border: string;\\\\n  accentBar: string;\\\\n  badgeBg: string;\\\\n  badgeText: string;\\\\\\n<truncated 6510 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Define unified theme card styles with solid black text and theme-specific pastel card backgrounds\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/theme.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating theme types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Upgrade theme tokens for cohesive theme-consistent cards and solid black text\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":115,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:53:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":4256,\"cache_read_tokens\":207395,\"output_tokens\":704,\"thinking\":\"**Examining Navigation.tsx**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into `Navigation.tsx` to address the dark/light mode switcher. The user\'s feedback is clear: ensure the moon icon is visible against any background. Therefore, I\'m adjusting the text to \\\"white moon\\\" when light mode is active. This will improve visibility and user experience.\\n\\n\\n**Verifying Icon Visibility**\\n\\nI\'ve located the dark/light mode button in both desktop and mobile headers. The implementation already uses a white moon icon in light mode within a dark background, addressing the user\'s concerns. Furthermore, the search bar and filter tabs in `Navigation.tsx` are next on my list.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/ThemeIllustrations.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing ThemeIllustrations\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check ThemeIllustrations banner text styling\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":117,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:53:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":8326,\"cache_read_tokens\":211452,\"output_tokens\":3871,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Text Presentation**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the `ThemeHeroIllustration` component. Specifically, I\'m focusing on line 168, the `<h2>` tag, and the text rendered in screenshot 1. I\'m noting the font, size, color, and spacing attributes, paying close attention to how they contribute to the visual presentation. This initial analysis is helping me understand the design choices made.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Light/Dark Mode**\\n\\nI\'ve fixed the `dark:` mode misfiring. Now, it\'s explicitly controlled by the `.dark` cla\\n<truncated 692 bytes>\\nloring bold color pairings with good contrast.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Theme Styles**\\n\\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing the new design specifications. In `WritingCard.tsx`, I\'m actively using the active theme\'s styling for background and border, with bolder colors. The titles will be jet black, bold, and extra large in light mode, and white in dark mode. The excerpt text is now true black in light mode, and a solid gray in dark mode. I\'m prioritizing optimal contrast, and modern aesthetics, as instructed.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_to_file\",\"args\":{\"CodeContent\":\"\\\"import React from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { ThemeMotifIcon } from \'./ThemeIllustrations\';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  Star,\\n<truncated 9249 bytes>\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update WritingCard to strictly follow active theme styling with pure solid black text and tactile borders\\\"\",\"Overwrite\":\"true\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/WritingCard.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Writing WritingCard component\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update WritingCard with theme-consistent palette and solid black text\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":119,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:54:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":4165,\"cache_read_tokens\":219986,\"output_tokens\":141,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"250\",\"StartLine\":\"170\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect dark mode switcher in Navigation.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":121,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:54:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":4111,\"cache_read_tokens\":221925,\"output_tokens\":3325,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Code Fragments**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining specific code snippets, focusing on the conditional rendering of light/dark mode icons. I\'m especially interested in how the `mode` variable dictates which icon, a moon or sun, gets displayed. I\'ve now scrutinized the mobile implementation of this logic. I\'m focusing on the differences.\\n\\n\\n**Refining UI Component Design**\\n\\nI\'ve significantly updated the dark/light mode toggle button design for both mobile and desktop. I am prioritizing visibility. The Moon ic\\n<truncated 8 bytes>\\nses white text for clarity and contrast. I\'ve also incorporated a visually distinct button background for both light and dark mode states.\\n\\n\\n**Optimizing Visual Consistency**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI consistency, specifically analyzing the visual presentation of the light/dark mode switch. I see that in light mode, the light mode navigation bar has black text, but this should be explicitly set for all links. The button, when in light mode, now utilizes a dark badge and a white moon for maximum contrast.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update dark/light mode toggle with white moon in light mode and high contrast nav links\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"252\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Change switcher to white moon in light mode and crisp black text for navigation\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"            {/* Dark / Light Toggle */}\\\\n            <button\\\\n              onClick={toggleMode}\\\\n              className={`w-9 h-9 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center transition-all shadow-xs border-2 ${\\\\n                mode === \'light\'\\\\n       \\n<truncated 3969 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"179\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"            {/* Dark / Light Toggle */}\\\\n            <button\\\\n              onClick={toggleMode}\\\\n              className=\\\\\\\"w-9 h-9 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200 bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 hover:bg-zinc-200\\n<truncated 3583 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating Navigation\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Replace dark/light toggle with white moon in light mode\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":123,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:54:34Z\",\"input_tokens\":5854,\"cache_read_tokens\":226004,\"output_tokens\":166,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/ThemeIllustrations.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"220\",\"StartLine\":\"155\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing ThemeHeroIllustration\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View ThemeHeroIllustration code\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":125,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:54:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2137,\"cache_read_tokens\":231763,\"output_tokens\":8184,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Text Elements**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on pinpointing specific text elements within the `ThemeHeroIllustration` component, specifically lines 168 and 171. I\'m noting the use of classes like `font-display-chic`, `text-xl`, and the interplay of color and font weights. I\'m trying to see what these different text elements can do together.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Banner Aesthetics**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on enhancing the banner designs. I\'m aiming for bolder, richer aesthetics. The goal is a captivating coquette blush gradient with a 3px berry border for Coquette, an electric indigo palette for Y2K, and rich matcha hues. I\'m focusing on text color contrasts and font-weight adjustments to ensure readability and visual appeal within each theme.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update ThemeHeroIllustration with bold borders, deep black readable text, and saturated badges\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"345\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Make hero banner text pure black and contrast-rich\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export const ThemeHeroIllustration: React.FC<{ themeId: AestheticThemeId }> = ({ themeId }) => {\\\\n  if (themeId === \'coquette\') {\\\\n    return (\\\\n      <div className=\\\\\\\"relative w-full h-32 md:h-36 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-r from-[#FFE0EC\\n<truncated 9788 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"159\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export const ThemeHeroIllustration: React.FC<{ themeId: AestheticThemeId }> = ({ themeId }) => {\\\\n  if (themeId === \'coquette\') {\\\\n    return (\\\\n      <div className=\\\\\\\"relative w-full h-32 md:h-36 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-r from-rose-100\\n<truncated 10382 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/ThemeIllustrations.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating ThemeHeroIllustration\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Upgrade hero banner with rich contrast and solid black text\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":127,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:55:44Z\",\"input_tokens\":15376,\"cache_read_tokens\":233478,\"output_tokens\":122,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"250\",\"StartLine\":\"170\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Inspect App.tsx heading and filter section\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":129,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:55:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":3962,\"cache_read_tokens\":246644,\"output_tokens\":4122,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the Code**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining specific lines in `src/App.tsx`, particularly focusing on the heading and paragraph elements. I\'m taking note of the class names, the text styling, and how they contribute to the overall visual presentation, including font choices and color schemes for light and dark modes. I\'m focusing on the interplay between different typographic elements.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Visual Styling**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on specific text elements and background colors within the application. I\'ve pinpointed several areas, like the subtitle and search input, where I can improve color contrast and visual impact. I\'ve adjusted the color assignments in specific lines like 210, 226 and the filter tabs to improve the user experience, particularly for dark mode. I\'m focusing on ensuring readability and a consistent design language.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Make Writing Log title, search input, and filter controls deeply contrasted with bold solid black text\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"285\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Make all text solid black and borders bold for maximum daylight visibility\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"            {/* Feed Control Bar: Title & Instant Search Bar */}\\\\n            <div className=\\\\\\\"flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-end justify-between gap-4 pb-2 border-b-3 border-black/20 dark:border-white/20\\\\\\\">\\\\n              <div>\\\\n                <h1 c\\n<truncated 6030 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"208\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"            {/* Feed Control Bar: Title & Instant Search Bar */}\\\\n            <div className=\\\\\\\"flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-end justify-between gap-4 pb-2 border-b-2 border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800\\\\\\\">\\\\n              <div>\\\\n                <h1 c\\n<truncated 6326 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Make feed controls solid black and ultra visible\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":131,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T13:56:21Z\",\"input_tok