  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Text Contrast**\n\nI\'ve been inspecting the light mode display and noticed inconsistencies. The `text-zinc-500`, `text-zinc-600`, and `text-zinc-400` classes are rendering text too faint and gray, as noted. This is impacting readability, and I think it may need adjustment. I\'m focusing on contrasting these colors to improve readability.\n\n\n**Refining Light Mode Adjustments**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the light mode display, specifically the dark/light mode switcher. The black icon on a black background is problematic, so I\'m considering changing the moon icon to white when in light mode for better visibility, as well as making the text more visible when its in light mode, as well as fixing issues with card design in light mode. I\'m also planning to improve contrast and enhance the aesthetic appeal, aiming for a bolder light mode with darker text and matching lighter card backgrounds for improved visibility and Genz aesthetic appeal.\n\n\n**Enhancing UI Element Design**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI element design for the light mode button. I\'m focusing on ensuring it has a solid background with a high-contrast border and a clear icon, like the `bg-zinc-900 hover:bg-zinc-800 text-white border-2 border-zinc-700 shadow-sm` class. The icon will be a white moon, and the text will be \"Moon\" or \"White Moon\", ensuring clear visibility on both desktop and mobile, avoiding black-on-black confusion. I am considering a pill design as well. I\'m also planning the dark mode counterpart to this element.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Text Readability**\n\nI\'ve decided to make all light mode text jet-black to improve readability, eliminating all instances of faint gray text across the board. The goal is to ensure a high-contrast experience, especially for elements like metadata, navigation links, and various labels. In dark mode, text will remain high-contrast white. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistent color schemes for cards, maintaining the theme\'s color while optimizing background shades for visibility.\n\n\n**Optimizing Theme Color Schemes**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into refining the visual themes. I\'m focusing on color matching and visibility across the themes, especially light mode. For the Coquette theme, I\'m setting a soft pastel blush pink app background, with lighter pink card backgrounds with a bolder rose berry border, and jet-black text for maximum readability. I\'m working on the Y2K theme to give it a strong Cyber starlight indigo / lilac / icy theme as well. I\'m making sure all this has high visibility and strong design.\n\n\n**Developing Theme Variations**\n\nI\'m now expanding the theme palette. For \"periwinkle\" light mode, I\'ve chosen an icy lilac mist background, light lavender cards with a bold electric indigo border and shadow, and jet-black text. \"Matcha\" features a light botanical foam background, creamy matcha cards with a deep ceremonial green border, and jet-black text. I\'m focusing on ensuring each theme has a distinct but readable aesthetic.\n\n\n"
