    thinking: "**Refactoring Navigation.tsx**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refactoring `src/components/Navigation.tsx`. My primary goal is to ensure a clean rewrite using `write_to_file`, to avoid any mismatches or truncation errors. I\'ve begun reviewing the existing file structure, specifically focusing on the imports, including React, `useTheme`, `useAuth`, `AppView`, and `AestheticThemeId`.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Switcher**\n\nI\'ve moved on to implementing the theme switcher within `Navigation.tsx`. The design includes a dropdown for theme selection and a dark/light toggle button. The code for the toggle uses lucide-react icons (`Sun`, `Moon`) with specific styling based on the current mode, using different class names for visual effects and accessibility (`aria-label`, `title`). I\'m now crafting the conditional rendering for each theme, ensuring smooth mode transitions.\n\n\n**Refining UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on fine-tuning the visual appearance and interactions of the theme and mode buttons within the mobile header. I\'m carefully reviewing the styling for light and dark modes, paying attention to the colors, borders, and transitions. I\'m focusing on the `onClick` event and updating the accessibility attributes of the button. I\'m also ensuring the icons and text are properly rendered in each mode.\n\n\n"
