  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Layout**\n\nI am currently focusing on the layout issues in the tablet view. I observed that the horizontal navigation items, like \"Writing Log,\" overflow and are clipped in the top bar. This suggests a potential responsiveness issue with the header design, especially on narrower screens, and needs some immediate attention.\n\n\n**Addressing the Overflow**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause of the horizontal overflow issue on tablet view, confirming the earlier observations. The current design in `Navigation.tsx` allocates too much width for the header\'s components within the `md` breakpoint range. The combination of the brand/offline badge, the navigation links, and the utility buttons creates a wider element than the screen can handle, leading to clipping and overflow. I\'m thinking of strategies to make it responsive.\n\n\n**Investigating Visual Overflow**\n\nI\'m now diving into the mobile view, specifically Image 2, and seeing overflow issues in the \"Connect with a Penpal\" section. The \"+ Add Friend\" button is hanging outside the card\'s rounded border, indicating horizontal overflow. The issue stems from the combination of input field\'s width and button size within a limited card width, even when the input has `flex-1`. I\'m going to explore a few adjustments.\n\n\n**Refining UI Adjustments**\n\nI\'ve examined the overflow issue with the \"+ Add Friend\" button on mobile. The input field and button are still clashing, and I see now that they should stack cleanly on smaller screens. I am making the design update so that the button stacks on smaller screens, keeping everything within the card\'s boundaries. I\'ll test the mobile response.\n\n\n**Designing the Author\'s Note**\n\nI am thinking about a new feature: an author\'s note dispatcher. This would allow the author to write a personalized message with a title, content, target audience, and dispatch it to users. The notes would be stored and displayed as a beautiful popup modal card when users open the app, and would feature aesthetic theming. I am considering different themes to match our aesthetics.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_466346"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\",\"EndLine\":140,\"StartLine\":50,\"toolAction\":\"Viewing Navigation top bar structure\",\"toolSummary\":\"Check Navigation top bar responsiveness\"}"
