 in how the `inputPenpalId` is being handled and transformed to uppercase, using `toUpperCase()`. I\'m considering the implications of this case transformation within the broader context of the component\'s functionality, and how this relates to user input and backend logic.\\n\\n\\n**Refactoring the PenpalHub**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on the visual layout of the PenpalHub component, specifically addressing the overflow issue on smaller screens. I\'ve updated lines 143-175 to incorporate `min-w-0 flex-1 w-full` for the input, restructuring the container to `flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-2`, and adjusting the button to `w-full sm:w-auto justify-center`. Also, I\'ve added `overflow-hidden` to the card container.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Fix mobile Add Friend button overflow in PenpalHub.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"176\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Make input and button wrap on mobile with min-w-0 and responsive flex\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"        {/* Card 2: Add Penpal Form */}\\\\n        <div className=\\\\\\\"p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border-3 border-black/20 dark:border-zinc-800 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-[4px_4px_0px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,1)] dark:shadow-none overflow-hidden\\n<truncated 2008 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"142\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"        {/* Card 2: Add Penpal Form */}\\\\n        <div className=\\\\\\\"p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900 border-3 border-black/20 dark:border-zinc-800 flex flex-col justify-between shadow-[4px_4px_0px_0px_rgba(0,0,0,1)] dark:shadow-none\\\\\\\">\\\\n          <\\n<truncated 1921 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/components/PenpalHub.tsx\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Fixing mobile Add Friend button overflow\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Fix mobile Add Friend button overflow in PenpalHub.tsx\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":314,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:09:24Z\",\"input_tokens\":2962,\"cache_read_tokens\":251397,\"output_tokens\":1155,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Tablet Display**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the tablet view header specifically, and noticed a potential layout issue. The horizontal arrangement of items in Image 1 feels cramped. The code snippet with `className=\\\"hidden md:block ...\\\"` suggests this is a display-specific problem. My current focus is to refine the `max-w-6xl` and spacing within the container, perhaps adjusting the `justify-between` and `gap-` values to improve readability and visual flow on tablets.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Tablet Layout**\\n\\nI\'ve \\n<truncated 435 bytes>\\nt navigation bar specifically. My goal is to ensure it fits perfectly without overflow across a variety of tablet screen sizes, specifically between 768px-1023px. To achieve this, I plan to set the header width to `w-full max-w-full overflow-hidden`. The challenge is to optimize the layout of the brand wordmark and the navigation items, ensuring each are legible within that space. I\'ll focus on fine-tuning spacing and potentially employing responsive font sizes, using `max-w-6xl` as a frame of reference.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"230\",\"StartLine\":\"50\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing Navigation.tsx top bar\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check Navigation lines 50-230\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}"
