    user_requests: "i want a web app, mainly for mobile devices but it should be clean in every design, take care to design separate clean designs for each device type and stuff from the start as doing it in the end doesnt make sense for tracking poems or short stories or just creative writing in general, sign up and sign in using google account, and i want an admin role with complete access, logging type of ui and on click should take me to the writing, i want excellent ui and smooth navigation with dark mode support, also the user should be able to color their own notes with custom themes and categories for better organization. and the writing should be displayed as cards, atleast selectable with some content like the name, author, date of writing, how many likes (they will called \'stars\') and the total number of comments for each entry. Finally, ensure the search functionality is lightning fast. Also, implement an offline mode so users can access their notes anytime. This should sync seamlessly across all devices once an internet connection is established. the themes should be fully customizable, including a dark and light mode for comfort, maybe if its easier we can just give them color options for a personalized user experience and not fully customisable in the true scences, and icons and neat designs included in the themes, like coquette bows, stars or minimalist shapes that match user preferences. This will help ensure the interface feels cohesive and visually appealing. a very big focus is ui and the ease of use and how visually appealing itll be as the actual functionality is not that heavy, we want genz focussed designs, which are sleek and quirky and still look polished. This should also include a dark mode and custom widgets for customization. also have documentation thatll teach me cleanly, about app dev and general things to think about and learn. keep the coding part simple, dont overbuild or overcomplicate. i can use free vercel and free supabase tiers for this, in the start. implement neatly, figure out what u need to think about, plan aggresively and implement\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "<clarifying-answers>\nQ: Which visual theme and icon set should be the primary default style for the app?\nA: Coquette, Y2K stars, matcha, and midnight dark vibes\nQ: How would you prefer the writing and editing interface to be presented?\nA: rich visual cards with mood tags, read time, word count and stats, writing in it should look visually pleasing too. the usp of the webapp will be its feel good factor\nQ: How should the built-in app development documentation and learning guide be structured?\nA: recommended works, but it shouldnt be public access. only for the developer, so figure out how only i will have access, maybe if the gmail sign up is through hiox2004@gmail.com then developer mode, and from there i can add or remove more developers\n</clarifying-answers>"
    user_requests: "for the users we will have drafts and publishes, and we can set up profiles, and add \"penpals\" by uniquely generated ids, display name, profile picture, a get to know me section. the writing can be in draft, published, share with friends. also we should be able to print the writing work with the same clean ui visible and download. the developer mode should get god mode access where they can view the drafts too (ethical moderation) we will mention this in the privacy policy towards launch. the developer should get full display access and account information too. but other users should only get to see display name and other in the webapp data, never the gmail.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "Proceed\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: proceed\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/086428c3-15a4-45b7-9111-0f1b8defc21e/implementation_plan.md\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "i think the lightmode colors make it hard for viewers to read, change after analysis. improve on the designs and making it look and fit better. currently its not even visible, and i want to be make the themes a bit bolder too, with designs of respective theme being more unique and not just a color share properly think of ideas and implement. replace emojis with icons from libraries, bolder designs, take ur time and carefully focus only on ui and designing, actually make a design after refering to other products with cute designs, with drawing on them according to the theme. genz humanlike art designs"
    user_requests: "okay so cant see black icon on black bg, change the text to white moon when in light mode. for the dark/light mode switcher\n\n- also in lightmode we have text in grey? we cant see make the color of text black, and also dont make the color of cards switch, keep it consistent with the theme, the cards should have the themes color and a shade of it as the bg for the card, but think about color matching and visibility of the colors. i added the screenshots of light mode, change color of text to make it visible and card designs to make it genz aesthetic friendly, and in light mode maybe we make the theme work more bolder and darker shade, with a matching lighter shade bgs i guess, u can figure it out but we want massive improvements in the visibiliy and design. we can be bold and make the visibility more theme focussed"
    user_requests: "in tablet view and 2nd img in mobile view, ui fixes. but good job i like the design now.\n\nI want a section note from the author which i can send person customised message i can write and send from dev mode. basically will be the popup page and closes onces closed, and disappears (need the animation too neatly) clean ui for that too, make it the most well worked card which gets shown according to the theme selected."
