  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Checking the Build Success**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the initial build has completed successfully. I\'ve moved on to verification, with the primary goal to enable the author to send custom messages. I\'m focusing on the `DevAcademy.tsx` component, where I\'ll be adding a dedicated tab to facilitate this functionality.\n\n\n**Adding the Author Note Tab**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Author\'s Note Dispatcher \360\237\222\214\" tab into `DevAcademy.tsx`, specifically within the existing tab structure around lines 185-235. The goal is to provide a user-friendly interface for crafting and sending custom notes. I\'m focusing on features such as note title inputs, category selection with badges, and a flexible recipient system. This includes both broadcasting to all users and targeting specific individuals with name/ID lookup. I\'m aiming for a balance of intuitive design and feature richness.\n\n\n**Implementing Note Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed note controls. I\'ve focused on allowing editable notes specifically for the Super Admin, which includes note content and a \"Dispatch Note Now\" button. This button handles saving, clearing dismissals, and displaying a success notification. I also added a \"Preview Card in Active Theme\" button to open the `AuthorNoteModal`. I\'m also adding controls to view/change the active note\'s status, target audience, and provide options to reset dismissals or deactivate it. I\'m taking another look at `App.tsx` next.\n\n\n**Integrating the Note Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating `AuthorNoteModal` into the application flow within `App.tsx`. I\'ve added state management for `activeAuthorNote` and `isAuthorNoteOpen`. I\'m checking if an active note exists on mount and determining if it should be displayed based on dismissal status and target audience. Upon dismissal or closure, I\'m setting the `StorageService` to dismiss the note, and setting `isAuthorNoteOpen` to false. Finally, I\'m going to add a visual indicator, like a \"\360\237\222\214 Note from the Author\" banner, on the main feed/navigation to ensure consistent access to author notes.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_355840"
      name: "view_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"AbsolutePath\":\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\",\"EndLine\":160,\"StartLine\":50,\"toolAction\":\"Viewing Navigation.tsx tablet header\",\"toolSummary\":\"View Navigation tablet classes 50-160\"}"
