  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising UI Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refining the UI components within `Navigation.tsx`, specifically the desktop/tablet header. I\'m tweaking the responsive design to ensure optimal rendering on tablets (`md:max-lg`). I\'m refining the padding and text size, along with button sizing, so they are correct.\n\n\n**Adjusting Theme Switcher**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the theme switcher\'s visual subtleties. Specifically, I am refining the button\'s appearance. I\'m focusing on the responsive sizing and styling. I am also adjusting the button text to suit. I\'m focusing on the border, shadow, and transition effects. I\'m also ensuring the moon and sun icons align with the color scheme in both light and dark modes.\n\n\n**Refining Profile Button**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the profile button within the UI. I\'m making several visual adjustments to ensure it aligns with the overall design. I am now optimizing the avatar\'s appearance, including refining the ring around the avatar. I\'m also ensuring the text truncates correctly on the button. I\'m focusing on border, shadow, and transition effects.\n\n\n**Optimizing Mobile Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the mobile top bar\'s layout. Specifically, I\'m refining the mode switcher button\'s styling and functionality to ensure a seamless experience. I\'m also addressing the brand wordmark to optimize its appearance and responsiveness within the mobile context.\n\n\n**Refining Navigation Elements**\n\nI\'m now revising the visual styling of the top bar\'s `ThemeMotifIcon` and button components. I am paying close attention to the border styles, transition effects, and ensuring the color contrast is correct between light and dark modes, and the icons scale correctly. I\'m also looking at the profile avatar, and updating the surrounding styling to fit.\n\n\n"
