  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding New Tab Feature**\n\nI\'ve made great strides in adding the \"Author\'s Note Dispatcher\" tab to `DevAcademy.tsx`. I\'ve updated the `activeTab` type to include \'author_note\'. Now, I\'m working on the tab bar, starting with the necessary button incorporating the `Mail` icon. I\'m focusing on ensuring it integrates seamlessly within the existing structure.\n\n\n**Designing Tab Content**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing the content for the \"Author Note Dispatcher\" tab. I\'m aiming for an elegant header featuring the title \"Author\'s Note & Personal Dispatch Engine\" and a descriptive subtitle. The layout will be a two-column structure for desktop, stacking on mobile, split into \"Compose & Dispatch New Note\" and \"Existing Notes\".\n\n\n**Defining Note Controls**\n\nI\'m deep in the specifics of the Author Note Dispatcher tab\'s content. I\'m finalizing the left column, defining note composition controls: Penpal ID/Recipient input, author details, the rich text area for note content, and the action buttons for dispatch and preview. In the right column, I\'m designing the active note controls: a mini preview card, status and target audience badges, and quick testing tools for previews, reset dismissal, deactivation, and restoration. I\'m incorporating the AuthorNoteModal preview element.\n\n\n**Integrating Preview Functionality**\n\nI\'ve integrated the `AuthorNoteModal` into `DevAcademy.tsx` to facilitate direct developer previews. Additionally, I\'m now integrating logic within `App.tsx` to conditionally display a preview modal. This is based on whether an author note is active, not dismissed, and appropriately targeted to the current user. I am using the state variables `activeAuthorNote` and `isAuthorNoteModalOpen`, along with StorageService calls, for this.\n\n\n"
