  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented the **Note from the Author** system and refined the **Tablet & Mobile UI** layouts:\n\n### 1. \"Note from the Author\" Thematic Pop-Up Card\n* **Theme-Specific Card Aesthetics**:\n  * **Coquette Blush**: Soft rosewater gradient with a ruby red border, handcrafted silk bow and vintage wax seal stamp, and postal ribbon accents.\n  * **Cyber Y2K**: Iridescent lavender and cloud-silver gradient with an electric indigo border, holographic chrome starburst badge, and cyber coordinates `[ + ]`.\n  * **Matcha Latte**: Soothing botanical steamed foam gradient with deep ceremonial green border, hand-drawn tea leaf seal, and serene literary proportions.\n  * **Midnight Muse**: Dreamy royal lilac gradient in light mode with a deep royal purple border, crescent moon seal, and celestial constellation sparkles.\n* **Smooth Animations & Folding Exit**:\n  * Integrated spring-based pop-up entrance animation with a backdrop blur.\n  * When closing or clicking **\"Fold Letter & Continue\"**, the modal neatly folds away and disappears, storing the dismissal state so it never nags users.\n* **Interactive Main Feed Access**:\n  * Added a dedicated themed letter banner on the main feed so users can reopen and reread the author\'s note anytime.\n\n### 2. Developer Mode Dispatcher (`Dev Academy`)\n* **Author Note Dispatcher Tab**: Added a dedicated management panel in Dev Mode with:\n  * **Custom Message Editor**: Form to customize the subject, prose body, category tags (e.g. *Creator Dispatch*, *Midnight Whisper*, *Behind The Scenes*), and author signature.\n  * **Personal Penpal Targeting**: Toggle between broadcasting to all writers or sending a personal letter targeted to a specific penpal (e.g. Clara Delacroix, Julian K.).\n  * **Live Preview Button**: Instantly tests and displays the modal card in the currently selected aesthetic theme.\n  * **Testing Controls**: Includes quick actions to reset dismissals for self-testing, deactivate notes (silent mode), or restore the default welcome letter.\n\n### 3. Tablet & Mobile UI Refinements\n* **Mobile Top Bar**:\n  * Converted the theme mode switcher into a compact square icon button (displaying the high-contrast White Moon in light mode and Sun in dark mode), preventing overflow and collisions on narrower devices.\n  * Added title truncation protection so the brand name and action buttons have generous spacing.\n* **Tablet App Bar**:\n  * Streamlined top bar actions for tablet viewports (768px\342\200\2231024px) by hiding redundant long text labels and preserving high-contrast icon buttons, preventing wrapping or header clipping.\n* **Responsive Card & Feed Layouts**:\n  * Made the `WritingCard` footer and action buttons wrap cleanly so author information never collides with interaction buttons.\n  * Updated hero banner heights to responsive minimum heights (`min-h-[124px] md:min-h-[140px] h-auto`) to guarantee zero text clipping on compact screens.\n  * Improved the filter and format bars with fluid responsive wrapping for tablets and phones."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Current Progress**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the linting and build processes have completed without errors. I\'ve now begun reviewing all accomplishments in response to the user\'s prompt, specifically focusing on the fixes implemented for the tablet and mobile UI. Navigation adjustments, including gap refinements and link optimizations, are top of mind. The Secondary button\'s text is now being examined.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Elements**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously refining the UI for different screen sizes. I\'ve successfully implemented `hidden lg:inline` for key text elements, ensuring a clean and uncluttered display across larger screens. The mode switcher is now a concise square button on mobile, replacing the cumbersome text. I\'ve also implemented responsive `min-heights` for hero banners and updated the filter and type bar\'s flex properties. The writing card footer is now responsive.\n\n\n**Developing New Modal Functionality**\n\nI\'ve just finished implementing a beautifully themed `AuthorNoteModal.tsx` component, creating unique cards for each of the four themes with custom seals and animations. The modal boasts high-contrast typography, an elegant font pairing, and even an author verification badge, all powered by `motion/react` for smooth transitions. I also integrated this modal into Developer Mode, adding a dedicated tab with full customization options.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have implemented the **Note from the Author** system and refined the **Tablet & Mobile UI** layouts:\n\n### 1. \"Note from the Author\" Thematic Pop-Up Card\n* **Theme-Specific Card Aesthetics**:\n  * **Coquette Blush**: Soft rosewater gradient with a ruby red border, handcrafted silk bow and vintage wax seal stamp, and postal ribbon accents.\n  * **Cyber Y2K**: Iridescent lavender and cloud-silver gradient with an electric indigo border, holographic chrome starburst badge, and cyber coordinates `[ + ]`.\n  * **Matcha Latte**: Soothing botanical steamed foam gradient with deep ceremonial green border, hand-drawn tea leaf seal, and serene literary proportions.\n  * **Midnight Muse**: Dreamy royal lilac gradient in light mode with a deep royal purple border, crescent moon seal, and celestial constellation sparkles.\n* **Smooth Animations & Folding Exit**:\n  * Integrated spring-based pop-up entrance animation with a backdrop blur.\n  * When closing or clicking **\"Fold Letter & Continue\"**, the modal neatly folds away and disappears, storing the dismissal state so it never nags users.\n* **Interactive Main Feed Access**:\n  * Added a dedicated themed letter banner on the main feed so users can reopen and reread the author\'s note anytime.\n\n### 2. Developer Mode Dispatcher (`Dev Academy`)\n* **Author Note Dispatcher Tab**: Added a dedicated management panel in Dev Mode with:\n  * **Custom Message Editor**: Form to customize the subject, prose body, category tags (e.g. *Creator Dispatch*, *Midnight Whisper*, *Behind The Scenes*), and author signature.\n  * **Personal Penpal Targeting**: Toggle between broadcasting to all writers or sending a personal letter targeted to a specific penpal (e.g. Clara Delacroix, Julian K.).\n  * **Live Preview Button**: Instantly tests and displays the modal card in the currently selected aesthetic theme.\n  * **Testing Controls**: Includes quick actions to reset dismissals for self-testing, deactivate notes (silent mode), or restore the default welcome letter.\n\n### 3. Tablet & Mobile UI Refinements\n* **Mobile Top Bar**:\n  * Converted the theme mode switcher into a compact square icon button (displaying the high-contrast White Moon in light mode and Sun in dark mode), preventing overflow and collisions on narrower devices.\n  * Added title truncation protection so the brand name and action buttons have generous spacing.\n* **Tablet App Bar**:\n  * Streamlined top bar actions for tablet viewports (768px\342\200\2231024px) by hiding redundant long text labels and preserving high-contrast icon buttons, preventing wrapping or header clipping.\n* **Responsive Card & Feed Layouts**:\n  * Made the `WritingCard` footer and action buttons wrap cleanly so author information never collides with interaction buttons.\n  * Updated hero banner heights to responsive minimum heights (`min-h-[124px] md:min-h-[140px] h-auto`) to guarantee zero text clipping on compact screens.\n  * Improved the filter and format bars with fluid responsive wrapping for tablets and phones."
