    session_summary: "{\"step_index\":317,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:09:50Z\",\"input_tokens\":14667,\"cache_read_tokens\":18279,\"output_tokens\":431,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing the UI Freeze**\\n\\nI\'ve hit a wall. The compaction process stalled right at step 224 while looking at `WritingEditor.tsx`, specifically when processing the user\'s latest prompt about UI fixes for tablet and mobile views, a section note, and liking the design. The issue seems linked to that particular prompt/file combination.\\n\\n\\n**Designing the Note Popup**\\n\\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing a \\\"Note from the Author\\\" popup, a feature requested for the dev mode. My focus is on creating a polished, high-fidelity card with theme styling, clean animations, and responsiveness. This aligns closely with my frontend design skills. I\'m aiming for a user-friendly interface that feels premium and integrated. The popup will be closable and disappear neatly, with its state stored locally or within the dev mode store.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/src/components\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Listing components\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"List components in src\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":319,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:09:58Z\",\"input_tokens\":2270,\"cache_read_tokens\":31455,\"output_tokens\":55,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"compile_applet\",\"args\":{\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Compiling applet\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Check compile status\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":321,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":2199,\"cache_read_tokens\":31663,\"output_tokens\":169,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/DevAcademy.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"120\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing DevAcademy.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DevAcademy top lines\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":323,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":2120,\"cache_read_tokens\":33851,\"output_tokens\":97,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/DevAcademy.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"250\",\"StartLine\":\"121\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing DevAcademy tabs\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DevAcademy tabs 121-250\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":325,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":2684,\"cache_read_tokens\":35961,\"output_tokens\":952,\"thinking\":\"**Considering UI Refinements**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s specific requests for UI improvements. I\'m exploring how to implement the tablet and mobile view adjustments, ensuring that the second image is appropriately displayed in the mobile view. The design feedback is positive, so now I am concentrating on the proposed author\'s note section which needs to be added to the dev mode. The popup page that can be edited and sent is also on my mind.\\n\\n\\n**Focusing on Popup Functionality**\\n\\nI\'m now fully im\\n<truncated 258 bytes>\\nvision this as a primary, easy-to-use card in the interface.\\n\\n\\n**Designing Author\'s Note Details**\\n\\nI\'m working on the specifics of the author\'s note popup. I\'m focusing on the different elements: the potential titles (\\\"behind-the-scenes,\\\" \\\"update\\\"), the author signature and date, and optional stamps. I\'m also planning the \\\"Active / Sent\\\" status and how the developer will interact with it. The UI considerations are critical, the card has to render according to the selected theme and have clean UI design.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"160\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx lines 1-160\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":327,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:18Z\",\"input_tokens\":3353,\"cache_read_tokens\":38891,\"output_tokens\":95,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/App.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"320\",\"StartLine\":\"161\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing App.tsx middle lines\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View App.tsx layout 161-320\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":329,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:21Z\",\"input_tokens\":3158,\"cache_read_tokens\":42216,\"output_tokens\":264,\"thinking\":\"**Observing Device Views**\\n\\nI\'m now examining how the navigation component, specifically `Navigation.tsx`, adapts to different device sizes. The Tailwind breakpoints are crucial here, particularly the distinctions between hidden/flex states at larger and smaller screen sizes. I\'m focusing on the `hidden lg:flex` and `lg:hidden` logic and correlating it with screen width breakpoints.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"140\",\"StartLine\":\"60\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing Navigation breakpoints\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View Navigation responsive breakpoints\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":331,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:26Z\",\"input_tokens\":4085,\"cache_read_tokens\":43364,\"output_tokens\":93,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"320\",\"StartLine\":\"230\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing Navigation mobile header\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View Navigation lines 230-320\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":333,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:29Z\",\"input_tokens\":3922,\"cache_read_tokens\":45363,\"output_tokens\":94,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"60\",\"StartLine\":\"40\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing desktop header classes\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View desktop header class definition\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":335,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":2870,\"cache_read_tokens\":47207,\"output_tokens\":660,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Tablet View**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on the tablet view. I\'ve been examining the `Navigation.tsx` file and specifically the behavior within `hidden md:block`. The desktop/tablet top bar\'s layout is using `gap-8` and I\'m looking closely at how \\\"Zone 1\\\" and \\\"Zone 2\\\" components are rendered, especially concerning their hidden/flex behavior based on screen size.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Tablet Layout**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the tablet layout. The critical area is `className=\\\"flex items-center gap-7 text-sm font-black ...\\\"` with four primary items and the action buttons. I see a potential for overflow between 768px-900px tablet width because the gap is `gap-7` with many items. The current height `h-16` can cause issues. I\'m considering smaller gaps (`md:gap-3 lg:gap-6`), smaller font sizes (`text-xs lg:text-sm`), and hiding text in buttons on tablet screens (`hidden lg:inline`).\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/Navigation.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"392\",\"StartLine\":\"320\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing mobile bottom bar\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View mobile bottom bar lines 320-392\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":337,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:39Z\",\"input_tokens\":2135,\"cache_read_tokens\":50277,\"output_tokens\":200,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/ThemeIllustrations.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"225\",\"StartLine\":\"150\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing ThemeHeroIllustration\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View ThemeHeroIllustration 150-225\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":339,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:43Z\",\"input_tokens\":2168,\"cache_read_tokens\":52381,\"output_tokens\":112,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WritingCard.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing WritingCard.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View WritingCard lines 1-100\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":341,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:46Z\",\"input_tokens\":4022,\"cache_read_tokens\":52452,\"output_tokens\":95,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/WritingCard.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"209\",\"StartLine\":\"101\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing WritingCard bottom part\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View WritingCard lines 101-209\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":343,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:10:49Z\",\"input_tokens\":2232,\"cache_read_tokens\":56445,\"output_tokens\":1447,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing Mobile View**\\n\\nI\'ve been examining the layout of `WritingCard.tsx`, specifically lines 151-204, to understand the mobile view. On smaller screens, the author\'s details appear on the left, using a `min-w-0` structure with `gap-2.5`, while the star button is positioned on the right, employing a `px-2.5 py-1` style.\\n\\n\\n**Optimizing Mobile Layout**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the implications of adding comment, quick print, quick download, and delete buttons to the mobile view. Placing all five in a row ris\\n<truncated 1080 bytes>\\nlues to improve spacing and applying responsive text size adjustments. In the `Actions` section, I\'m hiding the text labels \\\"White Moon,\\\" \\\"New Piece\\\" and \\\"Theme\\\" to replace them with icons, ensuring these components fit and appear beautifully on tablet displays. I\'ve also incorporated specific hiding strategies for the offline badge, and ensuring the brand title truncates on smaller mobile screens. On the mobile layout, I\'m standardizing the theme and mode switcher button size to 36x36px with icons only.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/services/storage.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing storage.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View storage.ts lines 1-100\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":345,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:11:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":3456,\"cache_read_tokens\":59112,\"output_tokens\":128,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/services/storage.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"425\",\"StartLine\":\"350\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing storage.ts author note methods\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View storage.ts lines 350-425\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":347,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:11:05Z\",\"input_tokens\":3394,\"cache_read_tokens\":60455,\"output_tokens\":115,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types/writing.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing writing.ts types\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View writing.ts types lines 1-100\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":349,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:11:07Z\",\"input_tokens\":3107,\"cache_read_tokens\":61742,\"output_tokens\":2424,\"thinking\":\"**Refining AuthorNote Customization**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on enhancing the `AuthorNote` interface within `src/types/writing.ts` to enable personalized customization. Specifically, I\'m thinking about how to add support for target audience specification, to better tailor author notes. This is a crucial step for increasing the versatility of the writing tool.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing AuthorNote Features**\\n\\nI\'ve been further developing the `AuthorNote` interface, specifically focusing on the new fields. I\'m consider\\n<truncated 2896 bytes>\\ne tackled the navigation bar in `Navigation.tsx`, adjusting gaps and text sizes for a cleaner look on tablets. I\'m ensuring the \\\"New Piece\\\" button displays properly and the theme button is compact. For the feed control bar on tablets, I\'m implementing a clean flex-wrap to prevent horizontal overflow. Additionally, I\'m adapting the card grid on tablets to a 2-column layout and making sure the footer buttons remain compact and don\'t collide. Finally, I\'ve truncated the brand name text in the mobile header.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types/writing.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"66\",\"StartLine\":\"45\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing AuthorNote definition\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View AuthorNote in writing.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":351,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:11:26Z\",\"input_tokens\":2968,\"cache_read_tokens\":65620,\"output_tokens\":368,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Enhance AuthorNote interface with customization options\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"61\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add targetUserName, tag, and avatar fields to AuthorNote\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export interface AuthorNote {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  title: string;\\\\n  content: string;\\\\n  authorName: string;\\\\n  authorRole: string;\\\\n  authorAvatar?: string;\\\\n  targetAudience: \'all\' | \'penpals\' | string; // \'all\' or specific penpal ID / user email\\\\n  target\\n<truncated 252 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"52\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export interface AuthorNote {\\\\n  id: string;\\\\n  title: string;\\\\n  content: string;\\\\n  authorName: string;\\\\n  authorRole: string;\\\\n  targetAudience: \'all\' | \'penpals\' | string; // \'all\' or specific penpal ID\\\\n  createdAt: string;\\\\n  active: boolean;\\\\n}\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/writing.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating writing.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update AuthorNote type definition\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":353,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:11:37Z\",\"input_tokens\":2860,\"cache_read_tokens\":66453,\"output_tokens\":139,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/services/storage.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"25\",\"StartLine\":\"12\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE lines 12-25\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":355,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:11:45Z\",\"input_tokens\":2751,\"cache_read_tokens\":67182,\"output_tokens\":1283,\"thinking\":\"**Revising Author Note**\\n\\nI\'m currently focused on updating the `DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE` within `src/services/storage.ts`. Specifically, I\'m integrating a `AuthorNote` with an `id`, `title`, and `content`. I\'ve started defining these parameters.\\n\\n\\n**Defining Default AuthorNote**\\n\\nI\'ve incorporated the provided author details and crafted a default `AuthorNote` object. This includes welcome message, author name and role, avatar URL, target audience details, and creation metadata. Now, I\'m integrating these detai\\n<truncated 97 bytes>\\nhor note in storage. I\'m taking a close look at the data structure.\\n\\n\\n**Implementing Storage Updates**\\n\\nI\'ve integrated the `saveAuthorNote`, `clearAuthorNote`, `isNoteDismissed`, `dismissNote`, and `undismissNote` methods to handle storage and retrieval of author note data. This includes local storage handling for author notes and dismissal states, using `localStorage.setItem` and `localStorage.getItem` and handling potential errors. I\'m also including logic to clear dismissals upon author note updates.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Update DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE with avatar, targetUserName, and tag\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"24\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE fields\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export const DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE: AuthorNote = {\\\\n  id: \'note_welcome_001\',\\\\n  title: \'A Handwritten Note from the Creator \360\237\222\214\',\\\\n  content: \'Welcome to Velours & Verse. I designed this sanctuary for words that refuse to be rushed\342\200\224for verses scribbled \\n<truncated 611 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"14\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export const DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE: AuthorNote = {\\\\n  id: \'note_welcome_001\',\\\\n  title: \'A Handwritten Note from the Creator \360\237\222\214\',\\\\n  content: \'Welcome to Velours & Verse. I designed this sanctuary for words that refuse to be rushed\342\200\224for verses scribbled \\n<truncated 425 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/services/storage.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Updating storage.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Update DEFAULT_AUTHOR_NOTE in storage.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\",\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":357,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:11:56Z\",\"input_tokens\":3879,\"cac