  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Dynamic Backgrounds**\n\nI\'m currently focused on implementing dynamic background gradients for cards. The plan is to leverage CSS `background-clip` to achieve a glassmorphism effect, blending the theme\'s primary color with the content within the card. This should create visually appealing and adaptable card designs.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme-Based Gradients**\n\nI\'ve defined theme-specific dynamic gradients, blending colors for visual appeal, directly within `WritingCard.tsx`. These gradients, linked to aesthetic themes, use CSS `linear-gradient` to create light and dark variants. I am now working on applying these gradients based on the selected theme, creating a cohesive visual experience.\n\n\n**Refining Background Application**\n\nI\'ve updated the implementation to use theme-specific gradients. I am applying dynamic backgrounds to the `<article>` element based on the `mode` and `themeId`. Now, light and dark variants are chosen. I\'m leveraging CSS for backdrop blur and background clipping, specifically padding-box to preserve content visibility.\n\n\n"
