  }
  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed all requested refinements and expanded the developer platform:\n\n### 1. Tablet & Mobile Responsive UI Fixes\n- **Mobile View 2nd Image / Illustration**: The hand-drawn aesthetic vector illustration in `ThemeHeroIllustration` is now visible on mobile devices with proportional scaling (`w-16 sm:w-28 md:w-36`), perfectly fitting alongside the title without crowding.\n- **Tablet View Layout**: Refined header spacing and link gaps in `Navigation.tsx` and optimized button text visibility on medium viewports to prevent collisions or text clipping.\n\n### 2. \"Note from the Author\" Themed Pop-Up & Dispatcher\n- **Themed Pop-Up Card (`AuthorNoteModal`)**:\n  - Dynamically styles vectors, wax seals, borders, and typography to the active theme (Coquette Bow, Cyber Y2K Chrome Star, Matcha Botanical Leaf, Midnight Crescent).\n  - Smooth spring pop-up entry and neat folding exit animation via Framer Motion.\n  - Automatically saves dismissal state upon closing so it disappears as expected, while remaining re-openable from the feed\'s letter banner.\n- **Developer Mode Note Dispatcher**:\n  - Write custom titles, tags, and personalized messages.\n  - Choose between a universal broadcast or targeting specific Penpal IDs.\n  - Live preview modal before sending, with persistent storage and default reset.\n\n### 3. Glassmorphism Card Gradients with `background-clip`\n- Implemented dynamic linear gradients for writing cards tailored to each theme\'s primary color in both Light and Dark modes.\n- Applied CSS `background-clip: padding-box` with `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)` and a frosted sheen overlay to blend theme colors with the literary content while preserving solid jet-black text contrast.\n\n### 4. Developer Mode Scope Expansion & Icon-Only Access\n- **Icon-Only Access & Restricted Normal Users**:\n  - Removed the words \"Dev Academy\"; only the `ShieldCheck` icon is shown.\n  - For normal users, the icon is non-clickable with a locked tooltip (`cursor-not-allowed`, `aria-disabled=\"true\"`).\n  - Updated the mobile bottom bar to a 5-column layout with Profile and an icon-only Dev item.\n- **Expanded Developer Suite**:\n  - **Live Telemetry & Storage Quota Meter**: Calculates real browser memory footprint, percentage used of 5MB quota, and per-key allocation.\n  - **Chaos Network Simulator**: Trigger real `offline` and `online` browser events to test offline alerts and sync states live.\n  - **Batch Creative Seeder**: Generate synthesized masterpiece poems and stories with a single click.\n  - **WCAG AAA Contrast Bench**: Live swatch matrix verifying theme readability standards."
    thinking: "**Revising UI Adaptations**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refining the UI adaptations, particularly for tablet view. Specifically, I\'m working on scaling the header padding and gaps, as well as adapting icon-only elements. I\'m aiming to ensure a seamless and visually pleasing experience across different screen sizes.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Responsiveness**\n\nI\'ve been examining the responsiveness across different devices, especially how `hidden lg:inline` affects button labels and names to prevent wrapping. The search bar and status tabs now flex gracefully on tablets, and the writing card grid works smoothly. I\'ve also ensured the hand-drawn artwork scales correctly on mobile devices without any overflow or collision.\n\n\n**Designing Theme-Adaptive Elements**\n\nI\'ve just finished the `AuthorNoteModal.tsx` component, a theme-customized card with beautiful visuals for Coquette, Cyber Y2K, Matcha, and Midnight themes. It\'s a full pop-up with Framer Motion animations. Dismissal is handled permanently, and can be re-opened from the banner. I\'ve also added a \"Note from Author (Dispatcher) \360\237\222\214\" tab in Dev Mode, enabling customized titles, messages, and audience selection, complete with a live interactive preview for dispatch testing and saving.\n\n\n**Adding Persistent Notes**\n\nI\'ve added a \"Save Note\" button to make personalized welcome notes persist for their target audience, and a \"Restore Default Welcome Note\" for easy resetting. I\'ve also implemented dynamic, theme-based background gradients for the cards, achieving a glassmorphism effect. This is applied in both the `WritingCard.tsx` and `AuthorNoteModal.tsx` components, with light and dark mode support.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed all requested refinements and expanded the developer platform:\n\n### 1. Tablet & Mobile Responsive UI Fixes\n- **Mobile View 2nd Image / Illustration**: The hand-drawn aesthetic vector illustration in `ThemeHeroIllustration` is now visible on mobile devices with proportional scaling (`w-16 sm:w-28 md:w-36`), perfectly fitting alongside the title without crowding.\n- **Tablet View Layout**: Refined header spacing and link gaps in `Navigation.tsx` and optimized button text visibility on medium viewports to prevent collisions or text clipping.\n\n### 2. \"Note from the Author\" Themed Pop-Up & Dispatcher\n- **Themed Pop-Up Card (`AuthorNoteModal`)**:\n  - Dynamically styles vectors, wax seals, borders, and typography to the active theme (Coquette Bow, Cyber Y2K Chrome Star, Matcha Botanical Leaf, Midnight Crescent).\n  - Smooth spring pop-up entry and neat folding exit animation via Framer Motion.\n  - Automatically saves dismissal state upon closing so it disappears as expected, while remaining re-openable from the feed\'s letter banner.\n- **Developer Mode Note Dispatcher**:\n  - Write custom titles, tags, and personalized messages.\n  - Choose between a universal broadcast or targeting specific Penpal IDs.\n  - Live preview modal before sending, with persistent storage and default reset.\n\n### 3. Glassmorphism Card Gradients with `background-clip`\n- Implemented dynamic linear gradients for writing cards tailored to each theme\'s primary color in both Light and Dark modes.\n- Applied CSS `background-clip: padding-box` with `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)` and a frosted sheen overlay to blend theme colors with the literary content while preserving solid jet-black text contrast.\n\n### 4. Developer Mode Scope Expansion & Icon-Only Access\n- **Icon-Only Access & Restricted Normal Users**:\n  - Removed the words \"Dev Academy\"; only the `ShieldCheck` icon is shown.\n  - For normal users, the icon is non-clickable with a locked tooltip (`cursor-not-allowed`, `aria-disabled=\"true\"`).\n  - Updated the mobile bottom bar to a 5-column layout with Profile and an icon-only Dev item.\n- **Expanded Developer Suite**:\n  - **Live Telemetry & Storage Quota Meter**: Calculates real browser memory footprint, percentage used of 5MB quota, and per-key allocation.\n  - **Chaos Network Simulator**: Trigger real `offline` and `online` browser events to test offline alerts and sync states live.\n  - **Batch Creative Seeder**: Generate synthesized masterpiece poems and stories with a single click.\n  - **WCAG AAA Contrast Bench**: Live swatch matrix verifying theme readability standards."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 296701111
