d on implementing dynamic background gradients for cards based on the selected theme. I\'m leveraging CSS background-clip to achieve a glassmorphism effect, blending the theme\'s primary color with the content within. The goal is a visually appealing and thematically consistent UI element.\\n\\n\\n**Analyzing Glassmorphism Techniques**\\n\\nNow I\'m diving deeper into how `background-clip` works with dynamic gradients to achieve the glassmorphism effect. I\'m building gradient examples for various themes, like Coquette, Cyber Y2K, and Matcha. I need to ensure a smooth transition between light and dark modes, and I have found the correct gradient patterns.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/AuthorNoteModal.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"100\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing AuthorNoteModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View top of AuthorNoteModal.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":368,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:35:31Z\",\"input_tokens\":3228,\"cache_read_tokens\":59551,\"output_tokens\":98,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/AuthorNoteModal.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"253\",\"StartLine\":\"101\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing rest of AuthorNoteModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 101 to 253 of AuthorNoteModal.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":370,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:35:34Z\",\"input_tokens\":3496,\"cache_read_tokens\":62748,\"output_tokens\":301,\"thinking\":\"**Analyzing HandleClose Logic**\\n\\nI\'m now diving into the `AuthorNoteModal.tsx` file, specifically the `handleClose` function. I see the intention is to manage a closing animation by setting `isClosing` to true. A short delay (22ms) is introduced before resetting `isClosing` to false and then calling `onDismiss` and `onClose`.