  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Extending the UI**\n\nI\'m focusing on replicating the existing UI and card designs from the writing log across the Penpals Circle, Sound, Widgets, and DevMode sections. Additionally, I\'m integrating the same theming when written content is opened, aiming for visual consistency and a more polished presentation throughout the project.\n\n\n**Designing Consistent Themes**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the visual integration, specifically aiming for a consistent theme-based styling utility. This is to ensure a unified user experience across the `ReaderModal.tsx` and `PenpalHub.tsx`. I\'m focusing on the reader container design, author credit boxes, comments, and action bars, with theming, glassmorphism, and subtle details. The `PenpalHub.tsx`\'s hero banner is also being styled to match.\n\n\n**Visualizing New Components**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the UI\'s details. I\'ve designed dynamic theme gradients, glassmorphism, accent bars, and motif watermarks. My goal is a frosted glass sheen overlay on cards like the \"My Personal Penpal Identity\" card. Furthermore, I\'m integrating high-contrast elements into \"Connect with a Penpal\" cards, and theme-matching gradients in the \"My Penpal Circle\" cards. I\'m taking the same approach for the `SoundWidget.tsx` with similar styling elements.\n\n\n**Refining Card Styles**\n\nI\'m working on refining card designs, incorporating a frosted glass sheen, top accent bars, and motif watermarks. I\'m introducing themed progress bars with gradient glows matching the theme\'s primary color and streak badges. I\'m now integrating these styles into the \"Spark of Inspiration\" card, with a dynamic theme gradient, frosted glass sheen, top accent bar, and literary border for a beautiful blockquote.\n\nI\'m also applying these refinements to the `DevAcademy.tsx` components. This includes the hero banner, quick metrics, and writings stream item cards, focusing on dynamic theme gradients, glassmorphism, accent strips, and motif watermarks for a cohesive look. I\'m focusing on the Telemetry and Chaos Sandbox cards with the same styling elements.\n\n\n**Styling & Theme Gradients**\n\nI\'ve styled the Architecture and Curriculum cards to match the writing log\'s depth. I\'m now checking if theme gradients are already exported or shared as a helper. I see they are used in `WritingCard.tsx`.\n\n\n"
