E\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:47:55Z\",\"input_tokens\":2502,\"cache_read_tokens\":61361,\"output_tokens\":1858,\"thinking\":\"**Extending the UI**\\n\\nI\'m focusing on replicating the existing UI and card designs from the writing log across the Penpals Circle, Sound, Widgets, and DevMode sections. Additionally, I\'m integrating the same theming when written content is opened, aiming for visual consistency and a more polished presentation throughout the project.\\n\\n\\n**Designing Consistent Themes**\\n\\nI\'m now deep-diving into the visual integration, specifically aiming for a consistent theme-based styling utility. This is to ensure a unified\\n<truncated 1288 bytes>\\nis includes the hero banner, quick metrics, and writings stream item cards, focusing on dynamic theme gradients, glassmorphism, accent strips, and motif watermarks for a cohesive look. I\'m focusing on the Telemetry and Chaos Sandbox cards with the same styling elements.\\n\\n\\n**Styling & Theme Gradients**\\n\\nI\'ve styled the Architecture and Curriculum cards to match the writing log\'s depth. I\'m now checking if theme gradients are already exported or shared as a helper. I see they are used in `WritingCard.tsx`.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/types/theme.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"247\",\"StartLine\":\"190\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Viewing end of theme.ts\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View lines 190-247 of src/types/theme.ts\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"thinking\"]}\n{\"step_index\":371,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:48:10Z\",\"input_tokens\":3124,\"cache_read_tokens\":64338,\"output_tokens\":2866,\"thinking\":\"**Defining Theme Variables**\\n\\nI\'m currently working on incorporating `THEME_DYNAMIC_GRADIENTS` and a helper function, `getThemeGlassCardStyle`, directly into `src/types/theme.ts`. My focus is on defining the structure of `THEME_DYNAMIC_GRADIENTS` as a `Record<AestheticThemeId, { light: string; dark: string; }>` to ensure a consistent approach for managing gradients within different aesthetic themes.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Theme Definitions**\\n\\nI\'ve been further specifying the `AestheticThemeId` with example definitions for \'coquette\', \'y2k\', and \'matcha\', including their respective light and dark gradients, border glow colors, and accent colors. These concrete instances are intended to act as templates, ensuring visual consistency across various aesthetic selections. I\'m focusing on refining the specific values.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Export THEME_DYNAMIC_GRADIENTS and getThemeGlassCardStyle helper in theme.ts\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"247\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Add THEME_DYNAMIC_GRADIENTS and getThemeGlassCardStyle to theme.ts\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"export const CARD_TINT_OPTIONS: CardTintOption[] = [\\\\n  { id: \'default\', name: \'Theme Native\', colorDot: \'#BE185D\', accentBar: \'bg-zinc-950 dark:bg-white\' },\\\\n  { id: \'rose\', name: \'Rose Silk\', colorDot: \'#F43F5E\', accentBar: \'bg-rose-500\' },\\\\n  { id: \'st\\n<truncated 2353 bytes>\",\"StartLine\":\"239\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"export const CARD_TINT_OPTIONS: CardTintOption[] = [\\\\n  { id: \'default\', name: \'Theme Native\', colorDot: \'#BE185D\', accentBar: \'bg-zinc-950 dark:bg-white\' },\\\\n  { id: \'rose\', name: \'Rose Silk\', colorDot: \'#F43F5E\', accentBar: \'bg-rose-500\' },\\\\n  { id: \'st\\n<truncated 366 bytes>\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/src/types/theme.ts\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Exporting theme glass helpers\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add THEME_DYNAMIC_GRADIENTS and getThemeGlassCardStyle\\\"\"}}],\"truncated_fields\":[\"tool_calls\"]}\n{\"step_index\":373,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:48:28Z\",\"input_tokens\":4327,\"cache_read_tokens\":67586,\"output_tokens\":595,\"thinking\":\"**Revising ReaderModal**\\n\\nI\'m now focusing on revitalizing the look of `ReaderModal.tsx`. The current aesthetic is rather plain, so I\'m thinking of incorporating the established themes. My inspiration lies in the UI depth found in writing logs, especially for the cards. I\'m aiming for a consistent visual language across the whole interface.\\n\\n\\n**Refining Modal Aesthetics**\\n\\nI\'m now zeroing in on the finer visual details within the modal. I\'m focusing on dynamic gradients for the main reader window, driven by `getThemeGlassCardStyle`. I\'m also planning a frosted glass sheen overlay and a theme watermark in the header. The sticky top bar will be glassmorphic with thematic badges. Finally, the scrollable reader body requires a parchment-like appearance.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"view_file\",\"args\":{\"AbsolutePath\":\"\\\"/src/components/ReaderModal.tsx\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"110\",\"StartLine\":\"1\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Checking top of ReaderModal.tsx\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"View imports and top of ReaderModal.tsx\\\"\"}}]}\n{\"step_index\":375,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-10-13T16:48:35Z\",\"input_tokens\":2544,\"cache_read_tokens\":72037,\"output_tokens\":10313,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Infuse ReaderModal with dynamic theme gradients, glassmorphism depth, frosted sheen, and themed comment cards\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"343\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Update ReaderModal to adopt the writing log card aesthetic depth, dynamic gradients, and themed cards for content and reflections\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"import React, { useState } from \'react\';\\\\nimport { WritingPiece } from \'../types/writing\';\\\\nimport { useAuth } from \'../context/AuthContext\';\\\\nimport { useTheme } from \'../context/ThemeContext\';\\\\nimport { C