  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing User Accounts**\n\nI\'m revisiting the user accounts directory table within `DevAcademy.tsx`, specifically lines 570-620. I\'m focusing on the structure and presentation of this component, considering potential improvements in readability and user interaction. I\'m particularly interested in how we can enhance the organization and clarity of the data displayed in the table. I will need to iterate on this to ensure accessibility, too.\n\n\n**Designing User Interface**\n\nI\'m thinking about the user accounts directory; I want it so users can click to open account details. I\'m aiming for a clean UI that displays all data neatly from our database. The UI and card designs from the writing log seem like a good approach; I\'ll adapt that design for the user accounts and other sections of the project.\n\n\n**Adapting UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now adapting the UI elements from the writing logs to the user accounts directory. The WritingCard/log card\'s dynamic gradients, frosted glass depth, and accent bars are inspiring me. I want to bring that depth across the app. I\'m focusing on incorporating these design principles, including gradients, frosted glass effects, accent bars, and theme motifs into the user account directory table. I am also planning to apply this to all the cards.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Enhancements**\n\nI\'m working on styling the User Accounts Directory card with glassmorphism, dynamic gradients, and accent bars, drawing directly from the writing log card\'s depth. I intend to make each row interactive so they\'re clickable for more data. Clicking a user will open a modal called \"User Account Dossier & Database Record.\"\n\n\\n\\n\n\nThis modal will present a comprehensive view, including avatar, display name, Penpal ID with a copy button, private email, system ID, account role with a toggle for promotion/demotion, and membership timestamp. I\'m focusing on the formatting, too.\n\n\n**Expanding User Dossier**\n\nI\'m now expanding the \"User Account Dossier & Database Record\" modal with additional details. I\'m adding fields for favorite drink and literary quote, a daily writing goal with a progress indicator, and a \"Penpals Circle Network\" section displaying connected penpal IDs. I\'m also including a list of authored writings with details like title, type, status, and metrics like total words, pieces, and stars. I\'m also adding quick dev actions for easy testing and updates.\n\n\n"
