  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Modal**\n\nI\'m currently focused on lines 1434-1442. I\'m thinking we can render the full User Account Details Dossier Modal there alongside `AuthorNoteModal`. I\'m starting to design the modal component in `DevAcademy.tsx`. This version will include database fields. First up: the header. We need a dynamic accent bar matching the active theme.\n\n\n**Defining the UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the UI components for the User Account Details Modal. The header will feature the user\'s avatar with an online indicator, display name, Penpal ID with a copy button, a private Gmail tag with a lock icon, and their role badge, all topped off with a close button. The body will be split into two sections: account credentials and metadata, and then creative persona and preferences.\n\n\n**Expanding the Dossier**\n\nI\'m now diving into the user account details modal, focusing on expanding the dossier. I\'m adding a section for favorite quotes and daily writing goals, along with a progress bar. Next, I\'m designing the \"Penpal Circle Network\" section with connected penpal counts and chips. I\'m planning to display database writings authored, with total stats and a list of pieces with \"Read & Inspect\" buttons. Finally, I\'m including \"God Mode Actions\" such as \"Switch To / Test as This User.\"\n\n\n**Adding New Modal Actions**\n\nI\'ve added new modal actions! I\'ve incorporated a button that pre-fills the Author Note tab with this user\'s penpal ID or email and immediately switches to it, closing the modal. There\'s also a toggle to display the raw JSON record of the user object, formatted for readability, along with a copy button. I\'m moving on to consider role toggling for users.\n\nI\'m checking if the user role can be toggled. I\'m now creating a helper function to manage the dev role. It will update the user\'s role and database entry. I also want to prevent the removal of Super Admin status.\n\n\n**Implementing User Control Actions**\n\nI\'ve just implemented actions for user control! I\'ve included functions for updating the user directory with role changes and switching the active session to a different user, which I added to the modal functionality. I\'ve also incorporated targeted author note capabilities based on the selected user from the modal. I\'m also now reviewing the search and role filters for the User Accounts Directory.\n\n\n"
