    thinking: "**Analyzing Code Structure**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `DevAcademy.tsx` file, specifically lines 662-705. My current focus is on a code block that I think can be improved. I\'m considering replacing it with a new `div` component, styled with `glassStyle`, and which uses a more modern and readable approach. This will be the replacement.\n\n\n**Refining Component Design**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the specific styling and structure of this new `div`. My aim is to create a sleek visual appearance using a frosted glass sheen, accent strip, and watermark, all within the `div` element. I will be incorporating these design elements within the component. I\'m exploring how to best implement this, as well as ensure the watermark is rendered correctly.\n\n\n**Evaluating Code Efficiency**\n\nI\'m now looking at optimizing this section. Currently, the code uses a combination of `flex` and `gap` for layout, and specific classes for styling the text and icons. I believe I can simplify this to improve readability. I\'ll test new approaches, such as moving the icon rendering and text styling to a centralized function.\n\n\n**Assessing Component Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the search and filter controls. I will need to focus on how the input field interacts with the search icon. I will ensure this is properly styled, especially in dark mode, and that it is fully responsive, ensuring it works as a search function on different screen sizes. I\'m focusing on the input field\'s visual presentation and responsiveness.\n\n\n**Refining Filter Logic**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the filter logic. I\'ve been reviewing the interaction between the buttons and the `userRoleFilter` state. I\'m focusing on the conditional styling and the event handlers. I want to optimize the responsiveness of these buttons, focusing on how they change state based on user input, and ensure they look good in light and dark mode. I\'ll test different click behaviors and visual feedback options.\n\n\n**Optimizing Button Styling**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the styling of the filter buttons, specifically regarding their visual states in light and dark modes. I\'m making sure that the active state has a strong visual distinction using background and font variations, and that the inactive state has a clear, muted appearance. I\'m also ensuring the transitions between states are smooth and intuitive, providing immediate visual feedback to the user on their selection.\n\n\n**Improving User Display**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the user display logic, specifically the conditional rendering of the \"no users found\" message. I\'m assessing the interaction between the `filteredUsers` array and the `userSearchQuery` to refine the message\'s accuracy. I want to make sure it\'s clear and concise, providing accurate feedback. I will also incorporate an improved display for users based on the pieces, developer status, and total words.\n\n\n**Enhancing Accent Bar Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual enhancements for the accent bar. Specifically, I am refining the appearance of the accent strip at the top of the user card, ensuring it is visually consistent and improves on the existing implementation. I am looking at how this strip appears within the overall design, specifically its appearance when the user is a dev. I\'m focusing on the responsive layout and accessibility of this section.\n\n\n**Refining User Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the user\'s name is displayed within the card. Specifically, I\'m examining the conditional rendering of the \"Current Session\" badge and the styling of the name itself. I\'m prioritizing ensuring the name truncates correctly, especially in conjunction with the badge, and that the text color adapts seamlessly between light and dark modes. I\'m also ensuring the badge renders accurately.\n\n\n**Evaluating User Indicators**\n\nI\'m now examining the visual indicators for user roles and special statuses within each user card. I\'m focusing on the styling of the user ID, specifically how the `penpalId` is rendered, ensuring it\'s clear and distinguishable. I\'m also refining the display of the user\'s role (Developer/Writer) to improve clarity and visual hierarchy. I\'m also looking into handling the God Mode status indicator.\n\n\n**Optimizing Footer Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the layout and content of the user card footer, specifically the metrics and call-to-action elements. I\'m prioritizing clarity in the display of key information and the integration of a simplified, more direct call to action. I will refine the spacing and styling of these elements to improve visual hierarchy and ensure a cohesive look.\n\n\n**Refining Footer Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the layout and content of the user card footer, specifically the metrics and call-to-action elements. I\'m prioritizing clarity in the display of key information and the integration of a simplified, more direct call to action. I will refine the spacing and styling of these elements to improve visual hierarchy and ensure a cohesive look.\n\n\n**Designing Account Details**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on designing the Account Details Dossier Modal, triggered by `selectedUserForModal`. I\'m going through the data, reviewing fields such as `displayName`, `penpalId`, `email`, and user-specific details like `bio` and `favoriteDrink`. I\'m currently structuring the data to be rendered in a comprehensive and easily digestible way.\n\n\n"
