  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the User Modal**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the User Account Details Dossier Modal. Specifically, I\'m working through the logic to display a comprehensive database view when `selectedUserForModal` is not null. I\'m structuring this as a conditional render, accessing the user data when available.\n\n\n**Calculating User Stats**\n\nI\'ve been calculating user-specific stats now, filtering through \"pieces\" data. I\'m extracting authored words, star counts, and the number of drafts, published, and penpal pieces. I\'m also determining if the user is a dev, using an email comparison and their role, and checking if it\'s the current session user.\n\n\n**Refining the Modal UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the visual enhancements of the user modal. I\'m adding styling, including accent bars, frosted glass overlays, and thematic corner watermarks. I\'m also ensuring the design is responsive and adapts correctly to different screen sizes. I\'m giving focus to accessibility, particularly for visually impaired users.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Avatar Display**\n\nI\'m currently updating the user avatar display within the modal. I\'m focusing on the visual elements of the avatar itself. I\'m incorporating a shadow effect for depth, a border, and a developer indicator badge if applicable. I am ensuring that the avatar is a reasonable size and has a good default if an image is unavailable.\n\n\n**Updating User Roles**\n\nI\'m currently updating the display logic for user roles within the modal. I\'m focusing on the visual cues that highlight if a user is the active session holder and if they are a developer or a writer. I\'m using conditional styling to show this information using pills with specific colors and borders. The visual differentiation helps make the information more accessible and intuitive.\n\n\n**Displaying Contact Info**\n\nI\'m now integrating contact details into the user modal, specifically the penpal ID and email. I\'m focusing on providing a clean, accessible presentation with clear copy functionality for the penpal ID. I\'m also using visual cues like icons and color coding to enhance clarity and indicate if the information is secure or sensitive.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Close Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the closing mechanism for the user modal, focusing on user experience. I\'ve integrated a close button with an \'X\' icon. The button utilizes hover effects for better visual feedback, using transitions for a smoother interaction. I\'m ensuring it\'s clearly labeled for accessibility and easy identification. The structure includes both a visual \'X\' icon and descriptive text for a clearer prompt.\n\n\n**Presenting Database Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the database record details, focusing on system IDs within the user modal. I\'m displaying the \'profiles\' table with the internal system ID. I\'m also including a copy button for the ID for easy reference, styled for clarity and integration. This enhances quick access to system-level information.\n\n\n**Adding Account Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the account creation date and copy user ID within the modal. I\'ve designed the copy button to provide feedback with a checkmark upon clicking and a hover state. I am ensuring that the account creation date displays properly, formatted for user clarity. Both of these are crucial database details to easily share the account ID and see when the account was created.\n\n\n**Displaying Private Email**\n\nI\'m now integrating the private email address display within the modal, as well as the user\'s role. I\'m focusing on ensuring data security by including an emphasis on user role for visibility. I\'m styling this with a clear presentation that balances privacy with information accessibility.\n\n\n**Implementing Dev Role Toggle**\n\nI\'m now integrating the developer role toggle within the user modal, creating a button that allows developers to be promoted or demoted. I\'ve focused on styling it clearly to indicate its purpose, using the appropriate text based on the user\'s current role, along with hover effects. I\'m ensuring it functions correctly to modify a user\'s role.\n\n\n**Integrating User Bio & Quote**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s bio and favorite quote display within the modal. I\'m focusing on clean formatting. I\'m using distinct styling for the bio with italics and a literary font for emphasis. I\'m handling cases where the user hasn\'t provided this information with a default prompt. I am also conditionally rendering the quote, applying appropriate styling, and maintaining a clear layout.\n\n\n**Adding User Preferences**\n\nI\'m now integrating user preferences such as their favorite beverage and daily writing goal within the modal. I\'m utilizing icons for visual clarity and designing the layout with a two-column grid. I\'m providing styling, including rounded borders, background colors, and a clear presentation of the information. I\'m handling default values gracefully if these preferences aren\'t set.\n\n\n**Integrating User Goals**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s daily writing goal and total authored word count display within the modal. I\'m prioritizing data presentation and clarity. I\'m providing styling, including custom text and an icon for visual distinction. I\'m incorporating the total words authored to provide context. I\'m handling cases gracefully if the writing goal isn\'t set.\n\n\n**Displaying Penpal Connections**\n\nI\'m now integrating the display of penpal connections within the modal. I\'m focusing on showing the user\'s connected penpals using `user.penpalIds`. I\'m handling the edge case where there are no connections with a clear message. I\'m rendering a list of penpal IDs when connections exist, which involves matching the IDs with the full user details. The presentation will be clear and easily readable.\n\n\n**Displaying Penpal Details**\n\nI\'m now rendering the full details for penpals, pulling `matchedUser.displayName` and the `penpal.id`. I\'m using a conditional rendering for the avatar, and the penpal\'s name. I am styling this to be very clear.\n\n\n**Summarizing Authoring Stats**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s writing stats and word count into the modal. I\'m focusing on providing clear presentation. I\'m displaying the number of authored writings from the database, total words authored, draft count, and the number of published pieces. I am also showing the number of stars received. I\'ve designed the presentation to be organized and easily readable.\n\n\n**Presenting Piece Statistics**\n\nI\'m now integrating piece data into the user modal, and showing writing statistics. I\'m focusing on handling empty data states gracefully. I\'m providing a message for no pieces and using a scrollable display with a border for any data available. This ensures that the user interface is clean and informative.\n\n\n**Displaying Piece Data**\n\nI\'m now rendering piece data, focusing on displaying each piece\'s status (draft, penpals, published) and type (article, poem, etc.), as well as word count and creation date. I\'m styling this with Tailwind classes to create pills showing status and type, with visual cues.\n\n\n**Integrating Piece Actions**\n\nI\'m now integrating piece actions into the user modal, and focusing on user interactions. I\'m adding a \"Read\" button with an external link icon to allow users to open each piece. I\'m utilizing styling, hover effects and transitions. I\'m focusing on ensuring responsiveness, and clear presentation.\n\n\n**Adding God Mode Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating God Mode functionalities into the user modal for admin users, focusing on secure access. I\'ve included a styled toggle to activate \"God Mode\" operations. I am focusing on providing a clean UX that clearly displays this functionality.\nI\'m also adding a session switch button, and ensuring it performs as designed.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Author Functions**\n\nI\'m now integrating author-specific functions within the modal, specifically a dedicated author note and raw database JSON record toggle. I\'ve styled the \"Send Dedicated Author Note\" button, focusing on a clean appearance. I am also adding a button to view the raw JSON record, and styled that.\n\n\n**Adding JSON Record Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s raw JSON record view within the modal, focusing on data accessibility. I\'ve included a \"Copy JSON\" button that copies the formatted JSON to the clipboard upon clicking, providing a success message for feedback, and I am dynamically displaying the formatted JSON data in a preformatted block. I\'ve designed the display with styling for clarity and easy reading, ensuring it\'s available and readable to all users.\n\n\n"
