  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying The Build**\n\nI\'ve got confirmation the build succeeded! Now I\'m focusing on user account details. I\'m imagining a smooth UI where clicking an account in the user accounts directory pulls up all relevant database info. I want a clean, easily navigable display of their details.\n\n\n**Expanding Account Details**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented interactive user cards in the directory! Clicking one now reveals the full User Account Details Dossier Modal. It\'s populated with every piece of info in the DB: avatar, display name, user ID (copyable!), penpal code, email (under dev mode), creation timestamp, role toggle, bio, favorite drink, quote, daily writing goal, penpal network, and a list of their writings. Each piece includes titles, statuses, word count, stars, and a \"Read\" button.\n\n\n**Integrating UI Design**\n\nI\'m now in the process of applying the writing log UI and card style across the entire project. This includes the Penpal Circle with its banner, profile cards, and correspondence cards. I\'m also updating the Sound & Widgets section with new cards for sound generators and the writing timer, along with the Dev Mode\'s header and metrics. Finally, I\'m working to make the \"read\" modal not bland using the existing themes.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_33922"
      name: "lint_applet"
      arguments_json: "{\"toolAction\":\"Linting codebase\",\"toolSummary\":\"Lint codebase\"}"
